repair. It plays a critical role during periods of rapid growth, making it particularly important for pregnant women and individuals in developmental stages. Additionally, F√≥lico is a medication that is recommended to be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. This dual significance highlights F√ìLICO's importance both as a vital nutrient and as a therapeutic agent.ESPIROLACTONA:Espirolactona is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort.FENITO√çNA:Fenito√≠na is an anticonvulsant medication that requires careful monitoring when administered with enteral nutrition due to its narrow therapeutic range. It is important to note that the plasma levels of Fenito√≠na can be significantly reduced when given alongside enteral nutrition, which necessitates close observation of its effectiveness. To minimize gastrointestinal discomfort, it is recommended that Fenito√≠na be taken with meals. Additionally, Fenito√≠na can impact vitamin D metabolism, which is an important consideration in its use.DICLOFENACO:Diclofenaco is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort.FLUTAMIDA:Flutamida is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort.DIFENHIDRAMINA:Difenhidramina is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort.GANCICLOVIR:Ganciclovir is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort.ETAMBUTOL:Etambutol is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort.G√ìME("ENTITY":INTERFER√ìN ALFA:Interfer√≥n alfa is a medication that can decrease appetite.CARBONATO DE LITIO:Carbonato de litio is a medication that can cause abnormal taste sensations.MERCAPTOPURINA:Mercaptopurina is a medication used in the treatment of certain types of cancer and autoimmune diseases.INDOMETACINA:Indometacina is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) used to treat pain and inflammation.METOPROLOL:Metoprolol is a beta-blocker used to treat high blood pressure and heart-related conditions.LISURIDA:Lisurida is a medication used to treat Parkinson's disease and other conditions related to dopamine deficiency.MORFINA:Morfina is a powerful opioid pain medication used to treat severe pain.METAMIZOL:Metamizol is a pain reliever and antipyretic used to treat pain and fever.NIMODIPINO:Nimodipino is a calcium channel blocker used to prevent brain damage following a subarachnoid hemorrhage.METILDOPA:Metildopa is an antihypertensive medication used to treat high blood pressure, especially in pregnancy.NORFLOXACINO:Norfloxacino is an antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections, particularly urinary tract infections.NITROFURANTO√çNA:Nitrofuranto√≠na is an antibiotic used to treat urinary tract infections.METILPREDNISOLONA:Metilprednisolona is a corticosteroid used to treat inflammation and autoimmune conditions.PROPRANOLOL:Propranolol is a beta-blocker used to treat high blood pressure, anxiety, and other conditions.NAPROXENO:Naproxeno is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) used to relieve pain and inflammation.PIRIZINAMIDA:Pirizinamida is an antibiotic used in the treatment of tuberculosis.RANITIDINA:Ranitidina is a medication that is primarily used to reduce stomach acid and treat conditions such as gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD). In exceptional cases, it can also be included in parenteral nutrition.RETINOL:Retinol is a form of vitamin A that plays a significant role in both dietary intake and skincare. It is associated with specific dietary recommendations for consumption, highlighting its importance in nutrition. Additionally, retinol is widely utilized in skincare products and dietary supplements, underscoring its versatility and effectiveness in promoting skin health and overall well-being.√ÅC. PIPEM√çDICO:√Åcido pipem√≠dico is an antibiotic used to treat urinary tract infections.PIROXICAM:Piroxicam is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) used to relieve pain and inflammation.TRIAMTERENO:Triamtereno is a potassium-sparing diuretic used to treat high blood pressure and fluid retention.TEOFILINA:Teofilina is a medication primarily used to treat respiratory diseases, including asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). Its therapeutic action can be influenced by dietary factors, as it is metabolized more quickly when a diet rich in proteins is consumed. This interaction may affect the effectiveness of the medication in managing respiratory conditions.VERAPAMILO RETARD:Verapamilo retard is a calcium channel blocker used to treat high blood pressure and heart conditions.TETRACICLINA:Tetraciclina is an antibiotic used to treat a variety of bacterial infections.√ÅC. VALPROICO:√Åcido valproico is a medication used to treat epilepsy and bipolar disorder.ZIDOVIDINA:Zidovudina is an antiretroviral medication used to treat HIV/AIDS.TUNEU7:Tuneu7 is the author or source of the modified document discussing drug interactions and dietary effects.TEMA 44:Tema 44 refers to the specific topic of interaction between diet and drugs as discussed in the document.EFECTO MASA:Efecto masa refers to the phenomenon where certain medications induce a feeling of fullness or satiety.ESTOMATITIS:Estomatitis refers to inflammation of the mucous membrane in the mouth, which can be a side effect of certain medications.DEFICIENCIA:Deficiencia refers to the lack of essential nutrients in the body, which can result from interactions with medications.EFECTO TOXICO:Efecto t√≥xico refers to the harmful effects that certain medications can have on the body, particularly on the gastrointestinal mucosa.ANTIVITAMINAS:Antivitaminas refers to substances that interfere with the action of vitamins in the body, often due to medication interactions.DIUR√âTICOS DE ASA:Diur√©ticos de asa are a class of diuretics that can lead to the loss of essential minerals.FITOESTR√ìGENOS:Fitoestr√≥genos are plant-derived compounds that can mimic estrogen and interact with certain medications.IPRIFLAVONA:Ipriflavona is a compound that acts as an inhibitor of certain enzymes and can interact with medications.)<|COMPLETE|>DIFENILHIDANTOINA:Difenilhidanto√≠na is a medication that can show signs of toxicity at therapeutic doses, particularly in cases of hipoalbuminemia.CUMAR√çNICOS:Cumar√≠nicos are a class of medications that can also exhibit toxicity at therapeutic doses, influenced by factors such as hipoalbuminemia.SOCIETY ESPA√ëOLA DE NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL Y PARENTERAL:DIETA RICA EN PROTE√çNAS:A high-protein diet can lead to increased production of cytochrome P450 enzymes, affecting the metabolism of certain medications like teofilina.DIETA RICA EN GRASAS:A high-fat diet can displace drugs bound to plasma proteins, potentially altering their effectiveness and absorption.DIETAS HIPOCAL√ìRICAS:Hypocaloric diets can increase protein catabolism, affecting the quantity and activity of enzymes responsible for drug metabolism.GASTROINTESTINAL TRACT:The gastrointestinal tract is the organ system that is affected by medications and can influence the tolerance of enteral nutrition.AEROFAGIA:Aerofagia is a condition that can be caused by high sorbitol content in liquid formulations, affecting tolerance to enteral nutrition.BEZOARES ESOF√ÅGICOS:Bezoares esof√°gicos are blockages that can occur in the esophagus due to interactions between medications and enteral nutrition.ANTIHISTAM√çNICOS:Antihistam√≠nicos are medications that can inhibit gastric motility.FENOTIACINAS:Fenotiacinas are medications that can inhibit gastric motility.ANTIPARKINSONIANOS:Antiparkinsonianos are medications that can inhibit gastric motility.INTERACCI√ìN FARMACODIN√ÅMICA:Interacci√≥n farmacodin√°mica occurs when there are alterations in the pharmacological action of a drug or the nutritional properties of a preparation without changes in pharmacokinetics.ADMINISTRACI√ìN CONJUNTA:Administraci√≥n conjunta refers to the simultaneous administration of drugs and enteral nutrition, which can lead to interactions affecting drug efficacy.PREVENCI√ìN DE INTERACCIONES:Prevenci√≥n de interacciones involves recommendations for administering medications to minimize interactions with enteral nutrition.FORMAS FARMAC√âUTICAS:Formas farmac√©uticas refer to the various pharmaceutical forms of medications that can affect their absorption and efficacy when administered with enteral nutrition.CUBIERTA ENTERICA:Cubierta ent√©rica is a type of pharmaceutical form designed to protect the active ingredient from degradation in the stomach.LIBERACI√ìN RETARDADA:Liberaci√≥n retardada refers to pharmaceutical forms that release the active ingredient slowly over time, which can be affected by crushing the medication.ABSORCI√ìN SUBLINGUAL:Absorci√≥n sublingual refers to the absorption of medications directly into the bloodstream through the tissues under the tongue, which can be altered by enteral nutrition.COMPRIMIDOS EFERVESCENTES:Comprimidos efervescentes are effervescent tablets that can be affected by the administration route and formulation when given with enteral nutrition.C√ÅPSULAS:C√°psulas are a form of medication that can contain granules with enteric coating, which should not be crushed to maintain their efficacy.ZUMO √ÅCIDO DE FRUTAS:Zumo √°cido de frutas is a liquid that can be used to administer certain medications through a feeding tube without compromising their integrity.)<|COMPLETE|>THOMSON14:Thomson14 is referenced as a source for guidelines on the administration of medications via enteral feeding tubes.DICUMAR√çNICOS:Dicumar√≠nicos are anticoagulant medications that need special precautions when administered with enteral nutrition.FORMULACIONES:Las formulaciones l√≠quidas son preparaciones que pueden contener nutrientes y f√°rmacos, y su composici√≥n puede influir en las interacciones que ocurren en el tracto gastrointestinal.SORBITO:AGENCIA ESPA√ëOLA DE PROTECCI√ìN DE LA SALUD EN EL DEPORTE:The Agency for the Protection of Health in Sports (AEPSAD) is responsible for promoting health and nutrition in sports in Spain.NIEVES PALACIOS GIL DE ANTU√ëANO:Nieves Palacios Gil de Antu√±ano is the Head of the Medicine, Endocrinology, and Nutrition Service at AEPSAD.FERNANDO GARC√çA P√âREZ-SEVILLANO:Fernando Garc√≠a P√©rez-Sevillano is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition based in Sevilla.HIP√ìCRATES:Hippocrates was an ancient Greek physician who emphasized the importance of diet and exercise for health.DIETA SANA:A healthy diet is a key component of maintaining good health and is emphasized in the context of physical activity.DEPORTISTA:A "DEPORTISTA" is an individual who actively engages in sports or physical exercise, with a strong emphasis on enhancing performance through proper training and nutrition. This athlete not only participates in physical activities but also adheres to specific dietary guidelines and hydration practices to achieve optimal results. The deportista is dedicated to improving their performance and overall health by following structured and regulated exercise routines. Their commitment to both physical activity and nutritional needs is essential for maximizing their athletic capabilities.ALIMENTACI√ìN EQUILIBRADA:La alimentaci√≥n equilibrada es un plan nutricional que satisface los requerimientos de energ√≠a necesarios para sostener el programa de competici√≥n y rendir a alto nivel.ENTRENAMIENTO DEPORTIVO:El entrenamiento deportivo es la pr√°ctica sistem√°tica, regular y progresiva del ejercicio f√≠sico para mejorar el rendimiento deportivo.SISTEMAS ENERG√âTICOS:Los sistemas energ√©ticos son las v√≠as utilizadas por el m√∫sculo esquel√©tico para cubrir sus demandas energ√©ticas durante el ejercicio.RENDIMIENTO:El rendimiento se refiere a la capacidad de un deportista para ejecutar su deporte de manera efectiva, influenciado por la nutrici√≥n y el entrenamiento.DEPORTISTAS:Deportistas refers to athletes who actively engage in physical activities and sports, focusing on improving their performance through various nutritional and physical aids. They are the primary subjects of the nutritional guidelines and recommendations discussed in the document. These individuals face health and performance challenges related to their available energy and are particularly susceptible to iron deficiency. As such, specific nutritional guidelines are essential for enhancing their performance and recovery.COMPETICIONES:Las competiciones son eventos deportivos donde los deportistas participan y pueden beneficiarse de una adecuada ingesta de hidratos de carbono.DIETA DEL DEPORTISTA:La dieta del deportista debe incluir una alta ingesta de hidratos de carbono para optimizar el rendimiento f√≠sico.RESERVAS DE GLUC√ìGENO:Las reservas de gluc√≥geno son la cantidad de gluc√≥geno almacenado en los m√∫sculos y el h√≠gado, crucial para el rendimiento deportivo.CLOSE ET AL:Close et al (2015) proposed practical guidelines for carbohydrate intake to optimize training loads with reduced muscle glycogen levelsCARGA DE ENTRENAMIENTO:Refers to the training load or intensity that an athlete undergoes during their training sessionsINGESTA DE HIDRATOS DE CARBONO:The process of consuming carbohydrates before, during, and after exercise to enhance performanceALTA INTENSIDAD:Refers to high-intensity training sessions that require specific carbohydrate intake for optimal performanceBAJA INTENSIDAD:Refers to low-intensity training sessions that have different carbohydrate intake requirementsPRODUCTOS PARA DEPORTISTAS:Los productos para deportistas incluyen una variedad de alimentos y bebidas dise√±ados para proporcionar carbohidratos de f√°cil consumo durante el ejercicio.GLUC√ìGENO MUSCULAR:El gluc√≥geno muscular es la forma en que se almacena la glucosa en los m√∫sculos, y es crucial para el rendimiento durante el ejercicio.S√çNTESIS DE GLUC√ìGENO:La s√≠ntesis de gluc√≥geno es el proceso mediante el cual el cuerpo repone el gluc√≥geno muscular y hep√°tico despu√©s del ejercicio, crucial para la recuperaci√≥n.TRANSPORTADORES DE GLUCOSA:Los transportadores de glucosa son prote√≠nas que facilitan la absorci√≥n de glucosa en el cuerpo, esenciales para el metabolismo de los carbohidratos.EJERCICIO DE ULTRARESISTENCIA:El ejercicio de ultrarresistencia se refiere a actividades f√≠sicas que duran m√°s de 2,5-3 horas, donde se requiere una ingesta elevada de carbohidratos para mantener el rendimiento.√çNDICE GLUC√âMICO:√çNDICE GLUC√âMICO is a measure that indicates how quickly a carbohydrate-containing food raises blood glucose levels. It classifies foods based on their impact on blood glucose levels, which is particularly important for the selection of carbohydrates after exercise.ALMACENAMIENTO DE GLUC√ìGENO:The process of glycogen storage is vital for athletes to maintain energy levels during prolonged physical activities.ADAPTACI√ìN:Adaptation refers to the physiological changes that occur in the body in response to training, improving performance and efficiency in energy use.STUART M. PHILLIPS:Stuart M. Phillips is a researcher who suggests optimal protein intake for muscle synthesis and hypertrophy.EJERCICIO DE FUERZA:Strength training exercises that promote muscle growth and increase protein synthesis.EJERCICIO DE RESISTENCIA:"EJERCICIO DE RESISTENCIA" refers to endurance exercises that are crucial for muscle development. These activities not only enhance physical performance but also consistently increase the protein requirements for individuals, particularly athletes. This type of exercise plays a fundamental role in promoting muscle growth and overall physical fitness.ENTRENAMIENTO DE FUERZA:El entrenamiento de fuerza es un tipo de ejercicio que, cuando se asocia con un incremento en la ingesta de prote√≠nas, puede conducir a un aumento del desarrollo muscular.TR√çADA DE LA MUJER DEPORTISTA:La tr√≠ada de la mujer deportista es un s√≠ndrome que incluye des√≥rdenes alimentarios, amenorrea y osteoporosis, afectando la salud de las deportistas.TERMORREGULACI√ìN:La termorregulaci√≥n es el proceso que el cuerpo utiliza para disipar el calor acumulado durante el ejercicio, crucial para el rendimiento deportivo.MENSTRUACI√ìN:La menstruaci√≥n puede aumentar la p√©rdida de hierro en algunas mujeres, contribuyendo a la deficiencia de hierro en deportistas.NUTRICI√ìN INADECUADA:La nutrici√≥n inadecuada, combinada con ejercicio intenso, puede llevar a un d√©ficit energ√©tico en deportistas.SUDOR:El sudor es un l√≠quido producido por las gl√°ndulas sudor√≠paras que ayuda a regular la temperatura corporal durante el ejercicio.CALAMBRES:Los calambres son contracciones musculares involuntarias que pueden ocurrir como resultado de la deshidrataci√≥n y el desequilibrio electrol√≠tico.CONSCIENCIA:La consciencia se refiere al estado de alerta y percepci√≥n de una persona, que puede verse afectado por la deshidrataci√≥n.ESTRATEGIA DE HIDRATACI√ìN:Una estrategia de hidrataci√≥n es un plan dise√±ado para asegurar que un deportista mantenga un nivel adecuado de l√≠quidos durante el ejercicio.RADIACI√ìN SOLAR:La radiaci√≥n solar es la energ√≠a emitida por el sol, que puede afectar la temperatura corporal y la necesidad de hidrataci√≥n durante el ejercicio.HUMEDAD:La humedad es la cantidad de vapor de agua en el aire, que puede afectar la hidrataci√≥n y el rendimiento de los deportistas durante el ejercicio.TEMPERATURA:TEMPERATURA refers to the degree of heat in the environment, which can significantly influence various factors, including the hydration needs of athletes during exercise. Additionally, TEMPERATURA encompasses the temperature conditions under which clinical nutrition products are processed, which is crucial for maintaining the stability and solubility of proteins and other ingredients in clinical nutrition formulations. Therefore, temperature is a critical element that affects both physical performance in sports and the quality of nutritional products.COMIT√â CIENT√çFICO EN ALIMENTACI√ìN HUMANA:The Scientific Committee on Human Nutrition (CCAH) of the European Union provides guidelines on the composition of foods and beverages for energy expenditure during intense muscular effort, especially for athletes.BEBIDAS DEPORTIVAS:BEBIDAS DEPORTIVAS, or sports drinks, are specially designed beverages intended for athletes to maintain proper hydroelectrolytic balance during physical activity. These drinks provide essential hydration and energy, supporting athletes in their performance and endurance while engaging in sports or exercise.GASTO DE GLUC√ìGENO MUSCULAR:Muscle glycogen expenditure refers to the use of stored carbohydrates in muscles during physical activity, which can be influenced by hydration and carbohydrate intake.CCAH:The Comisi√≥n de Alimentaci√≥n Humana (CCAH) is an organization dedicated to promoting health and nutrition, particularly in the context of athletic performance. CCAH advocates for specific guidelines concerning isotonic beverages, focusing on their osmolality to ensure optimal hydration and energy replenishment for athletes. Additionally, the organization has drafted a comprehensive report on the composition of foods and beverages designed to meet the energy expenditure needs of individuals engaged in intense muscular efforts, emphasizing the importance of proper nutrition in athletic training and performance.FEDERACI√ìN ESPA√ëOLA DE MEDICINA DEL DEPORTE:The Federaci√≥n Espa√±ola de Medicina del Deporte is a group that published a consensus document on nutrition in 2008, endorsing specific beverage compositions for athletes.ERGOGENIA:Ergogenia refers to methods and techniques aimed at enhancing physical and mental performance in sports.TAURINA:TAURINA, also known as taurine, is a sulfur-containing amino acid that plays a crucial role in various physiological functions. It is often discussed in nutritional contexts due to its potential benefits. In the realm of infant nutrition, TAURINA may be added to infant formulas to support immune function and promote gastrointestinal development. Additionally, taurine is recognized for its use among athletes, as it may enhance physical performance. Overall, TAURINA is significant for both developmental and performance-related applications.GINSENG:Ginseng is an herbal supplement that may be used by athletes to enhance performance.INOSINA:Inosine is a supplement that may be used by athletes to improve performance.T√â VERDE:Green tea is a beverage that may be consumed by athletes for its potential performance-enhancing properties.AGENTES ALCALINIZANTES:Alkalizing agents, such as bicarbonate, are used by athletes to improve performance and delay fatigue.SUPLEMENTOS PROTEICOS:Protein supplements are used by athletes to enhance muscle growth and recovery.BETA-HIDROXI-BETA-METILBUTIRATO:Beta-hydroxy-beta-methylbutyrate (HMB) is a supplement used by athletes to promote muscle growth and recovery.√ÅCIDO LINOL√âICO CONJUGADO:El √°cido linoleico conjugado (CLA) es un compuesto utilizado para la optimizaci√≥n del peso y la composici√≥n corporal.CART√çLAGO DE TIBUR√ìN:El cart√≠lago de tibur√≥n se utiliza para aumentar la resistencia a las lesiones y para la recuperaci√≥n de lesiones asociadas con el ejercicio.MUCOPOLISAC√ÅRIDOS:Los mucopolisac√°ridos son compuestos utilizados para la prevenci√≥n y recuperaci√≥n de lesiones en el √°mbito deportivo.ARNICA:La √°rnica es un compuesto utilizado para la recuperaci√≥n r√°pida y completa de lesiones asociadas con el ejercicio.VITAMINAS C Y E:Las vitaminas C y E son compuestos antioxidantes utilizados para optimizar la recuperaci√≥n postejercicio.PROVITAMINA A:La provitamina A es un antioxidante utilizado para mejorar la recuperaci√≥n tras el ejercicio.N-ACETIL L-CISTE√çNA:La N-acetil L-ciste√≠na es un compuesto utilizado para mejorar la recuperaci√≥n tras el ejercicio.BIOFLAVONOIDES:Los bioflavonoides son compuestos utilizados para optimizar la recuperaci√≥n postejercicio.EQUINACEA:La equinacea es un inmunomodulador utilizado para mejorar la recuperaci√≥n tras el ejercicio.ESPIRULINA:La espirulina es un suplemento utilizado para optimizar la recuperaci√≥n postejercicio.Œí-ALANINE:Œ≤-alanine is a nutritional supplement that can elevate muscle carnosine content, improving performance in high-intensity exercises.DOSIS DE MANTENIMIENTO:Dosis de mantenimiento refers to the daily dosage of supplements required to maintain satisfactory levels of phosphocreatine in the body.ALACTICO:BETA-HIDROXI-METIL-BUTIRATO:Beta-hidroxi-metil-butirato (HMB) is a compound derived from leucine that plays an anabolic role in muscle preservation and is used to reduce muscle catabolism during exercise.DIRECCI√ìN GENERAL DE SALUD Y PROTECCI√ìN DEL CONSUMIDOR:The Direcci√≥n General de Salud y Protecci√≥n del Consumidor is a European Commission body that oversees health and consumer protection, including nutritional guidelines.ALIMENTACI√ìN DEPORTIVA INTENSIVA:Alimentaci√≥n deportiva intensiva involves specialized dietary strategies aimed at enhancing athletic performance during high-intensity training or competition.ALIMENTACI√ìN DEPORTIVA REGENERADORA:Alimentaci√≥n deportiva regeneradora focuses on nutrition strategies that aid recovery after exercise, helping athletes restore energy and repair muscle.NUTRICI√ìN DEPORTIVA:Nutrici√≥n deportiva encompasses the dietary practices and nutritional strategies specifically designed to support athletes' performance and recovery.DEPORTISTAS DE √âLITE:Deportistas de √©lite are elite athletes who engage in high-level competition and have specific nutritional needs due to their intense training regimens.NIVEL DE ACTIVIDAD:Nivel de actividad refers to the intensity and frequency of physical exercise that athletes engage in, influencing their nutritional requirements.CONCENTRACIONES DE VITAMINA D:Concentraciones de vitamina D refer to the levels of vitamin D in the body, which are critical for athletes' health and performance.EFECTOS PERJUDICIALES:Efectos perjudiciales refer to the negative impacts on muscle function and overall health that can occur when vitamin D levels are insufficient.NUEVAS INVESTIGACIONES:Nuevas investigaciones refer to ongoing studies aimed at understanding the relationship between vitamin D and athletic performance.)<|COMPLETE|>HMB-CA:HMB-Ca is a form of Hydroxymethylbutyrate that is bound to calcium, mentioned in the context of nutritional supplementation for athletes.HMB-FA:HMB-FA is a free acid form of Hydroxymethylbutyrate, discussed as a nutritional supplement for optimizing athletic performance.PHILLIPS SM:Phillips SM is a researcher who has published studies on protein quality and its effects on muscle mass and weight loss in athletes.TAKANAMI Y:Takanami Y is a researcher who has investigated the benefits of vitamin E supplementation in endurance exercise.MACHEFER G:Machefer G is a researcher who has studied the impact of extreme running competitions on blood antioxidant defense capacity.VIITALA P:Viitala P is a researcher who has examined the relationship between vitamin E supplementation, exercise, and lipid peroxidation.PALACIOS N:Palacios N is a researcher who has contributed to various studies on nutritional ergogenic aids for athletes.CONSTANTINI NW:Constantini NW is a researcher focused on the iron status of highly active adolescents, particularly gymnasts.HOUTKOOPER L:Houtkooper L is a researcher who has explored eating disorders and disordered eating in athletes.SANBORN CHF:Sanborn ChF is a researcher who has studied disordered eating in female athletes.ANA ORTOL√Å BUIGUES:Ana Ortol√° Buigues is a doctor and co-author of a study focused on water metabolism in patients receiving artificial nutrition. She has made significant contributions to the field of enteral nutrition through her research and studies.LUIS √ÅNGEL CU√âLLAR OLMEDO:Luis √Ångel Cu√©llar Olmedo is a medical professional specializing in the field of nutrition, with a particular focus on parenteral nutrition and access routes for enteral nutrition. He is associated with the Servicio de Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n at Hospital Universitario R√≠o Hortega, where he applies his expertise to improve nutritional care for patients.CONCEPCI√ìN TERROBA LARUMBE:Concepci√≥n Terroba Larumbe is a medical professional specializing in nutrition, particularly in enteral and parenteral nutrition access methods. She is associated with the Servicio de Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n at Hospital Universitario R√≠o Hortega, where she contributes to discussions and advancements in the field of nutrition.ANA ALEJANDRA CORDERO VAQUERO:Ana Alejandra Cordero Vaquero is a medical professional who specializes in nutrition, particularly in enteral and parenteral nutrition. She is associated with the Servicio de Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n at Hospital Universitario R√≠o Hortega, where she applies her expertise in providing nutritional support to patients.INTERNATIONAL SOCIETY OF SPORTS NUTRITION:The International Society of Sports Nutrition is an organization that provides guidelines and position stands on sports nutrition topics, including beta-hydroxy-beta-methylbutyrate (HMB).SPORTS MEDICINE:Sports Medicine is a journal that focuses on the field of sports medicine, including research on dietary protein and its effects on athletes.STRENGTH & CONDITIONING RESEARCH:Strength & Conditioning Research is a journal that publishes studies on strength training, conditioning, and nutrition for athletes.EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF APPLIED PHYSIOLOGY:The European Journal of Applied Physiology publishes research on the physiological aspects of exercise and nutrition.ARCHIVOS DE MEDICINA DEL DEPORTE:Archivos de Medicina del Deporte is a journal that focuses on sports medicine and nutrition for athletes.CLINICAL SPORTS NUTRITION:Clinical Sports Nutrition is a book that provides comprehensive information on nutrition for athletes, including dietary strategies and supplementation.NUTRITION AND SANT√â IBERIA, S.L.:Nutrition and Sant√© Iberia, S.L. is a company that focuses on dietary products and nutritional support for athletes.ARCH MED DEPORTE:Arch Med Deporte is a journal that publishes research related to sports medicine and nutrition.JOURNAL OF THE INTERNATIONAL SOCIETY OF SPORTS NUTRITION:The Journal of the International Society of Sports Nutrition publishes research on sports nutrition and dietary supplements for athletes.NUTRITION & METABOLISM:ANA ORTOL√Å BUIGES:Ana Ortol√° Buiges is a prominent figure in the field of clinical nutrition, specializing in immunonutrition and artificial nutritional support. As a doctor with expertise in nutrition, she actively engages in discussions surrounding enteral nutrition. Additionally, she is recognized as an author and contributor to both clinical and parenteral nutrition, highlighting her significant involvement and contributions to advancing knowledge in these areas.CENTRO DE INVESTIGACI√ìN ENDOCRINOLOG√çA Y NUTRICI√ìN:Centro de Investigaci√≥n Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n is a research center affiliated with the University of Valladolid, focusing on nutrition and metabolism.METABOLISMO H√çDRICO:Metabolismo h√≠drico involves the processes of water balance and management in patients receiving artificial nutrition.NECESIDADES NUTRICIONALES:Las necesidades nutricionales son los requerimientos de nutrientes que pueden aumentar en ciertas condiciones m√©dicas, lo que puede llevar a la necesidad de nutrici√≥n enteral.DIARREA CUANTIOSA PERSISTENTE:La diarrea cuantiosa persistente es una condici√≥n caracterizada por evacuaciones intestinales frecuentes y abundantes que pueden afectar la salud del paciente.NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL EXCLUSIVA:La nutrici√≥n enteral exclusiva es un enfoque de tratamiento que utiliza solo nutrici√≥n enteral para pacientes con condiciones espec√≠ficas, como la enfermedad de Crohn pedi√°trica.COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS SEVERAS:Las complicaciones infecciosas severas son efectos adversos que pueden surgir de la nutrici√≥n parenteral, aumentando el riesgo de infecciones en pacientes.ENTERITIS AGUDA GRAVE:F√ìRMULAS DE NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL:Las f√≥rmulas de nutrici√≥n enteral son preparaciones dise√±adas para proporcionar nutrientes a pacientes a trav√©s de la alimentaci√≥n enteral, clasificadas en completas e incompletas nutricionalmente.DIARREAS:A condition that can be regulated with the use of specific nutritional formulasMALTODEXTRINA:Maltodextrina, also known as maltodextrin, is a carbohydrate that serves as a vital energy source in various nutritional formulations. It is commonly utilized in enteral nutrition products, where it plays a significant role in providing energy to individuals who require nutritional support.CASE√çNA HIDROLIZADA:Hydrolyzed casein, a protein source used in enteral nutritionAISLADO DE PROTE√çNA DE SOJA:Soy protein isolate, a protein source used in enteral nutritionFIBRAS:PREDI√ÅLISIS:La predi√°lisis es la fase anterior a la di√°lisis en pacientes con enfermedad renal cr√≥nica, donde se requiere un manejo nutricional espec√≠fico.OCFA:Obstructive Chronic Airflow Disease (OCFA) is a condition where specialized nutritional formulas may be indicated.FORMULAS NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional formulas are specialized products designed to meet the dietary needs of patients, particularly those unable to consume food orally.F√ìRMULA:F√ìRMULA es un sustituto de la leche materna utilizado para alimentar a los reci√©n nacidos, especialmente aquellos que son prematuros. Esta f√≥rmula est√° dise√±ada para satisfacer las necesidades nutricionales espec√≠ficas de estos infantes. Adem√°s, las f√≥rmulas de nutrici√≥n enteral son preparaciones que proporcionan nutrientes a pacientes que no pueden alimentarse por v√≠a oral, lo que resalta la versatilidad y la importancia de las f√≥rmulas en el √°mbito de la nutrici√≥n m√©dica y pedi√°trica.SUEROTERAPIA:La sueroterapia es un m√©todo de administraci√≥n de l√≠quidos y nutrientes a trav√©s de una v√≠a venosa, complementando la nutrici√≥n enteral.F√ìRMULA ESPECIAL:A specialized nutritional formula designed for patients with organ failure.F√ìRMULA ADAPTADA A PATOLOG√çA:A nutritional formula adapted to specific medical conditions.F√ìRMULA OLIGOM√âRICA:A type of nutritional formula that is partially hydrolyzed for easier absorption in patients with intestinal failure.F√ìRMULA NORMOPROTEICA:A nutritional formula containing a normal amount of protein, suitable for patients without severe stress.F√ìRMULA HIPERPROTEICA:A nutritional formula with a high protein content, used for patients under severe stress.F√ìRMULA NORMOCAL√ìRICA:A nutritional formula providing a normal caloric intake.F√ìRMULA HIPERCAL√ìRICA:A nutritional formula providing a high caloric intake for patients with increased energy needs.VAR√ìN DE 75 A√ëOS:A 75-year-old male patient admitted for medical treatment, potentially requiring nutritional support.NUTRICI√ìN CON JERINGA:A method of administering nutrition using a special syringe, typically delivering 200-300 ml per intake throughout the day.NUTRICI√ìN POR GRAVEDAD:A method of intermittent infusion that relies on gravity to regulate the flow of nutrition, typically administered 4-6 times a day.PRESCRIPCI√ìN DE NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL:The process of prescribing enteral nutrition, which must be standardized and precise to reduce errors in dispensing.MONITORIZACI√ìN DE NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL:The monitoring of enteral nutrition, focusing on the clinical and metabolic status of the patient and their tolerance to the nutritional preparation.VALORACI√ìN DE LA TOLERANCIA:The assessment of a patient's tolerance to enteral nutrition, which is crucial for effective treatment.NUTRICI√ìN INTERMITENTE:REQUERIMIENTOS PROTEICOS:Los requerimientos proteicos son la cantidad de prote√≠nas que el var√≥n de 75 a√±os necesita diariamente, que se ha establecido en 70 g/d√≠a.REQUERIMIENTOS H√çDRICOS:Los requerimientos h√≠dricos son la cantidad de l√≠quidos que el var√≥n de 75 a√±os necesita diariamente, que se ha establecido entre 2100-2800 ml/d√≠a.BOLOS:Los bolos son una forma de administraci√≥n de nutrici√≥n enteral en la que se administran cantidades espec√≠ficas de alimento en intervalos regulares.EVALUACI√ìN DE LA TOLERANCIA:La evaluaci√≥n de la tolerancia es un proceso importante para determinar c√≥mo el var√≥n de 75 a√±os est√° respondiendo a la nutrici√≥n enteral.S√çNTOMAS DEL PACIENTE:Los s√≠ntomas del paciente, como dolor abdominal y n√°useas, son indicadores que se eval√∫an para determinar la tolerancia a la nutrici√≥n enteral.VARIABLES ANTROPOM√âTRICAS:Las variables antropom√©tricas, como el peso y los per√≠metros, son medidas que se revisan semanalmente en el var√≥n de 75 a√±os para evaluar su estado nutricional.V√çA ORAL:V√çA ORAL refers to the method of nutrition that is being considered for a 75-year-old male patient once his condition allows for it. This approach aims to recover the oral feeding method, which some patients have transitioned to after ending their NPD (Nutritional Parenteral Diet) treatment.RESIDUO G√ÅSTRICO:El residuo g√°strico se refiere a la cantidad de alimento o l√≠quido que permanece en el est√≥mago despu√©s de la alimentaci√≥n. Este volumen de contenido es importante para evaluar la tolerancia a la nutrici√≥n enteral, ya que su presencia puede indicar problemas de tolerancia. En pacientes que reciben nutrici√≥n enteral, el residuo g√°strico se mide y se monitoriza para asegurar que el cuerpo est√° procesando adecuadamente los nutrientes.ESTRATEGIAS PARA REDUCIR EL RIESGO DE ASPIRACI√ìN:Son pr√°cticas recomendadas para minimizar el riesgo de aspiraci√≥n en pacientes que reciben nutrici√≥n enteral.BLOQUE SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO:VACIADO G√ÅSTRICO:El vaciado g√°strico es el proceso mediante el cual el contenido del est√≥mago se mueve hacia el intestino delgado, y es un factor cr√≠tico en la nutrici√≥n enteral.T√âCNICA DE ADMINISTRACI√ìN:La t√©cnica de administraci√≥n se refiere a los m√©todos utilizados para proporcionar nutrici√≥n enteral, incluyendo la posici√≥n del paciente y el ritmo de infusi√≥n.SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO:SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO refers to advanced nutritional support practices and protocols utilized in medical settings, particularly for patients in critical conditions. This approach encompasses various techniques aimed at managing the nutritional needs of patients, especially those requiring enteral and parenteral nutrition. It emphasizes the importance of catheter management and infection prevention to ensure patient safety and efficacy of nutritional support. Additionally, SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO focuses on the specific electrolyte and mineral requirements necessary for optimal patient care, while also addressing potential complications associated with parenteral nutrition. Overall, it plays a crucial role in influencing patient outcomes, including the management of conditions such as diarrhea.ANTIHIPERTENSIVOS:Antihypertensives are medications used to treat high blood pressure, which can have diarrhea as a side effect.COLINERGICOS:Cholinergics are drugs that can stimulate the parasympathetic nervous system and may cause diarrhea as a side effect.ANTIACIDOS CON MAGNESIO:Antacids containing magnesium can lead to diarrhea due to their laxative effect.ANTIDIABETICOS ORALES:Oral antidiabetic medications can cause gastrointestinal side effects, including diarrhea.INHIBIDORES DE LA RECAPTACION DE LA SEROTONINA:Serotonin reuptake inhibitors are antidepressants that can have gastrointestinal side effects, including diarrhea.FARMACOS QUIMIOTERAPICOS:Chemotherapeutic agents can cause various side effects, including diarrhea, due to their impact on rapidly dividing cells in the gastrointestinal tract.ANTIBIOTICOS:FASCITIS NECROTIZANTE:Severe infection of the soft tissue that leads to necrosis, often occurring in patients with compromised immune systems.BENZODIACEPINAS:A class of medications that can contribute to constipation in patients, particularly the elderly.OPI√ÅCEOS:Opioid medications that are commonly associated with causing constipation in patients.(N␀␀␀␀␀␀√Q␀␀␀␀␀␀wT␀␀␀␀␀␀ÁT␀␀␀␀␀␀iU␀␀␀␀␀␀␀V␀␀␀␀␀␀gV␀␀␀␀␀␀›V␀␀␀␀␀␀ùW␀␀␀␀␀␀X␀␀␀␀␀␀‰X␀␀␀␀␀␀qY␀␀␀␀␀␀‰Y␀␀␀␀␀␀wZ␀␀␀␀␀␀[␀␀␀␀␀␀”[␀␀␀␀␀␀c\␀␀␀␀␀␀Ï\␀␀␀␀␀␀õ]␀␀␀␀␀␀0^␀␀␀␀␀␀«^␀␀␀␀␀␀c_␀␀␀␀␀␀˜_␀␀␀␀␀␀˛_␀␀␀␀␀␀‘a␀␀␀␀␀␀Ec␀␀␀␀␀␀Âc␀␀␀␀␀␀≠e␀␀␀␀␀␀*f␀␀␀␀␀␀¬f␀␀␀␀␀␀<g␀␀␀␀␀␀‹g␀␀␀␀␀␀mh␀␀␀␀␀␀˝h␀␀␀␀␀␀∞i␀␀␀␀␀␀âk␀␀␀␀␀␀l␀␀␀␀␀␀l␀␀␀␀␀␀.n␀␀␀␀␀␀o␀␀␀␀␀␀œo␀␀␀␀␀␀<q␀␀␀␀␀␀Dq␀␀␀␀␀␀r␀␀␀␀␀␀™r␀␀␀␀␀␀Hs␀␀␀␀␀␀Âs␀␀␀␀␀␀Ñt␀␀␀␀␀␀(u␀␀␀␀␀␀∑u␀␀␀␀␀␀_v␀␀␀␀␀␀ıv␀␀␀␀␀␀Ñw␀␀␀␀␀␀(x␀␀␀␀␀␀:z␀␀␀␀␀␀
