áºŒƒ„º÷Èn=G1˝º∏ﬁ;ÏÊ√<a°ˇªçbÉ;ﬁºŸ)␀º~s{ºMDsºL„ZºtS<Ωlúº	 ÛºÓÁ§;ÖΩ/=∏øºööº·á1ºõ4CΩ)Ì4ΩqÒüª√,+ºıàº‰È*Ω…èÖ<Üá“;ïïº©Õ‹<†{<∂Ù©ºaßâ<&≥-<7ÜŒ<V!=éfΩ∏ﬁ<s¢ú:jº<¿+ ª¨ˆØ<œ%|<–u`<˙ñ=∑;›Ïë<”ÓΩ|± ºﬂ≈Äªmg4Ω‚◊=•˘ñªH7ºı´ó<-w†∫‚ΩèÄºwûT;ºWºÔ˛<cR¸;Yk@<"=ı´;âÿº6%∂ºFÜ
<2ä;‚!º/Pª§©≤<,˛º¬Ì˙ª–åûº#y¶<(+∫¢ÁÅºÕcÀªiµ÷º∞Äõ;˜<¸®∞<Cª.␀+<°o´;’ü;‚ˇá<æiôº'ΩÉd	<œd¨;|ºS∫<°o´ºÑùØªU®.Ωÿ=ÃÁ;íMá<∆é§<}/:p⁄aª97K=…ù= /ºHÅa=RY<¨Œ=;$⁄>º$⁄><±ÚÁºl–∫u{ã<≈>@<DæœªÚô<xÓ∏<˙æΩï;jªºƒ§Å=Ësñ<iÃî<_ﬂNªÍ¸ ªˇí”;¸Äæ<Sf<æzÕ<å=X
(=4$U<ƒÓ[=ùÂø<P¶Ïª@#0=òÈΩ›˝≈; º–≈ƒª/(ùº^.Rº∫∑ª;1ΩL"ãº⁄ä=x›ºA•;ñô<Dæœª}¬˛ªÿ±);JIúºz∞È<&ãª<6%6<B<¢Ω<§©2ºÀ‘<«HºB¸û;7M®∫ºê*ºKÇ¬;Ø0∑<ÔHΩºΩ5<{"title": "ALERGIAS ALIMENTARIAS:\"ALERGIAS ALIMENTARIAS\" refers to adverse reactions caused by the consumption of certain foods, mediated by the immune system. These food allergies represent a heterogeneous group of diseases characterized by immunological mechanisms, often manifesting in childhood and frequently resolving before adulthood. In predisposed individuals, food allergies can trigger severe immune responses to specific foods, leading to various clinical manifestations. These reactions may include immediate responses as well as delayed symptoms, depending on the type of immune response involved. A comprehensive medical history is essential to determine whether symptoms are indeed adverse reactions to particular foods. Food allergies are abnormal immune responses to antigens released in the digestive tract, primarily mediated by Immunoglobulin E (IgE), which can result in adverse reactions to specific food items."}{"title": "INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS:INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS refer to adverse reactions to certain foods that do not involve the immune system, distinguishing them from food allergies. These intolerances are often linked to enzyme deficiencies, such as lactose intolerance, where the body lacks the necessary enzymes to properly digest specific foods. The reactions associated with food intolerances are non-immune and can lead to various symptoms, particularly gastrointestinal issues, as well as other health problems. In summary, INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS are characterized by their non-IgE mediated nature, resulting in a range of adverse effects without the involvement of the immune response."}{"title": "URTICARIA:Urticaria is a skin reaction characterized by hives, often associated with allergic responses to food."}{"title": "ANAFLAXIA AL\u00c9RGICA ORAL:Anafilaxia al\u00e9rgica oral is a severe allergic reaction that occurs after the ingestion of certain foods."}{"title": "BRONCOESPASMO:Broncoespasmo is a condition characterized by the tightening of the muscles around the airways, which can be triggered by food allergies."}{"title": "RINITIS:Rinitis is an inflammation of the nasal mucous membrane, which can be caused by food allergies."}{"title": "ANGIOEDEMA:Angioedema is a condition involving swelling beneath the skin, often related to allergic reactions to food."}{"title": "ENTEROCOLITIS INDUCIDA POR PROTE\u00cdNAS DE LA DIETA:Enterocolitis inducida por prote\u00ednas de la dieta is a gastrointestinal condition triggered by dietary proteins, often seen in food allergies."}{"title": "TOXINAS BACTERIANAS:Toxinas bacterianas are harmful substances produced by bacteria that can cause adverse reactions to food."}{"title": "SOCIETY OF ALLERGOLOGY AND CLINICAL IMMUNOLOGY:The Society of Allergology and Clinical Immunology (SEAIC) is an organization that conducts epidemiological studies on allergies and intolerances in Spain."}{"title": "ALLERGIES:Allergies are adverse reactions to certain foods that can affect 1-3% of the global population, with higher prevalence in children."}{"title": "GLUTEN INTOLERANCE:Gluten intolerance affects about 1% of the general population and is a type of food intolerance."}{"title": "GENETIC PREDISPOSITION:Genetic predisposition refers to the inherited likelihood of developing food allergies, influenced by environmental factors."}{"title": "IG\u00c9:IgE es un anticuerpo que juega un papel crucial en las reacciones al\u00e9rgicas, siendo secretado por el sistema inmune en respuesta a al\u00e9rgenos alimentarios."}{"title": "CELULAS DE LANGERHANS:Las c\u00e9lulas de Langerhans son c\u00e9lulas del sistema inmunol\u00f3gico que captan al\u00e9rgenos a trav\u00e9s de la barrera cut\u00e1nea y son importantes en la respuesta al\u00e9rgica."}{"title": "LINFOCITOS TH2:Los linfocitos TH2 son un tipo de c\u00e9lula T que se activan en respuesta a al\u00e9rgenos y son responsables de la producci\u00f3n de IgE."}{"title": "LINFOCITOS TH1:Los linfocitos TH1 son un tipo de c\u00e9lula T que se activan en la tolerancia a al\u00e9rgenos cuando se ingieren por v\u00eda oral."}{"title": "FLORA BACTERIANA SAPR\u00d3FITA:La flora bacteriana sapr\u00f3fita puede modular la respuesta inmunol\u00f3gica y es importante en el fen\u00f3meno de la tolerancia a al\u00e9rgenos alimentarios."}{"title": "ANT\u00cdGENOS:Los ant\u00edgenos son sustancias que provocan una respuesta inmune, liberados en el tubo digestivo y que pueden causar alergias alimentarias."}{"title": "RESPUESTA INMUNE:La respuesta inmune es la reacci\u00f3n del sistema inmunol\u00f3gico a ant\u00edgenos, que puede ser anormal en el caso de alergias alimentarias."}{"title": "MEDIO AMBIENTE:El medio ambiente se refiere a las condiciones externas que pueden influir en la salud y predisposici\u00f3n a enfermedades, incluyendo alergias."}{"title": "POLIMORFISMOS:Los polimorfismos son variaciones en el ADN que pueden influir en la predisposici\u00f3n a enfermedades, incluyendo alergias alimentarias."}{"title": "GENOMA:"}{"title": "SENSIBILIDAD AL GLUTEN:La sensibilidad al gluten es un diagn\u00f3stico controvertido que se refiere a una condici\u00f3n que puede causar s\u00edntomas gastrointestinales en personas que no padecen enfermedad cel\u00edaca. Esta condici\u00f3n puede mejorar con la exclusi\u00f3n del gluten, lo que alivia s\u00edntomas como dolores de cabeza y abdominales. Se ha estudiado en ensayos cl\u00ednicos controlados para comprender su impacto, especialmente en relaci\u00f3n con el s\u00edndrome de colon irritable."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS IGE:ANTICUERPOS IGE son anticuerpos que se producen en respuesta a al\u00e9rgenos y son fundamentales en el diagn\u00f3stico de alergias alimentarias mediadas por IgE. Estas prote\u00ednas del sistema inmunol\u00f3gico desempe\u00f1an un papel crucial en las reacciones al\u00e9rgicas, ya que su presencia indica una respuesta del organismo a sustancias que pueden causar alergias."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS IGG:Los anticuerpos IgG son un tipo de anticuerpo que puede indicar exposici\u00f3n a ciertos alimentos, pero no necesariamente una reacci\u00f3n al\u00e9rgica."}{"title": "ALERGIAS E INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS:The entity \"ALERGIAS E INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS\" encompasses the diagnosis and treatment of food allergies and intolerances. It includes discussions on the mechanisms of tolerance and desensitization, as well as the symptoms associated with these conditions. Additionally, the entity covers various diagnostic tests used to identify food allergies and intolerances, providing a comprehensive overview of the subject."}{"title": "BENZOATOS:Benzoatos are additives found in various foods, including blueberries and plums, and are used in food preservation."}{"title": "GLUTAMATO MONOS\u00d3DICO:Glutamato monos\u00f3dico, also known as MSG, is a flavor enhancer widely used in Asian cuisine and can cause specific food reactions."}{"title": "TARTRACINA:Tartracina is a colorant associated with asthma and chronic urticaria, commonly found in various food products."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DEL RESTAURANTE CHINO:A condition affecting a small percentage of the adult population, characterized by symptoms after consuming high amounts of MSG."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE ALERGIA ORAL:A condition caused by plant proteins that cross-react with airborne allergens, leading to oral and pharyngeal symptoms."}{"title": "ANAFILAXIA GASTROINTESTINAL:A severe allergic reaction occurring in the gastrointestinal tract, often presenting with nausea and abdominal pain."}{"title": "ESOFAGITIS EOSINOF\u00cdLICA AL\u00c9RGICA:An allergic condition that typically appears in childhood or adolescence, often resistant to conventional treatment for gastroesophageal reflux."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO ACETILSALIC\u00cdLICO:\u00c1cido acetilsalic\u00edlico, commonly known as acetylsalicylic acid or aspirin, is a medication that is often used for its analgesic, anti-inflammatory, and antipyretic properties. It is important for individuals who are sensitive to benzoates to be cautious, as acetylsalicylic acid can cause sensitivity in these individuals. Additionally, to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort, it is recommended that \u00c1cido acetilsalic\u00edlico be taken with meals."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO BENZOICO:Benzoic acid is a natural preservative found in some fermented products and is also used as a food additive."}{"title": "SULFITOS:"}{"title": "ALERGIA ALIMENTARIA:ALERGIA ALIMENTARIA se refiere a una reacci\u00f3n adversa del sistema inmunol\u00f3gico a ciertos alimentos. Esta condici\u00f3n puede ser mediada por inmunoglobulina E (IgE) o por mecanismos celulares. Los s\u00edntomas de la alergia alimentaria pueden manifestarse de diversas formas, incluyendo problemas gastrointestinales, reacciones cut\u00e1neas y s\u00edntomas respiratorios. Para diagnosticar esta alergia, es necesario realizar pruebas espec\u00edficas y eliminar de la dieta los alimentos que se sospecha puedan estar causando la reacci\u00f3n."}{"title": "URTICARIA AGUDA:Urticaria aguda es una reacci\u00f3n cut\u00e1nea mediada por IgE que se manifiesta a trav\u00e9s de habones inflamatorios y pruriginosos. Esta condici\u00f3n suele estar relacionada con la ingesta de al\u00e9rgenos."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNA DE LA LECHE DE VACA:La prote\u00edna de la leche de vaca es un al\u00e9rgeno com\u00fan que puede causar reacciones adversas en lactantes, incluyendo enterocolitis inducida por la prote\u00edna de los alimentos."}{"title": "ANAFILAXIA:Anafilaxia es una reacci\u00f3n severa de hipersensibilidad que puede comprometer la vida, siendo la alergia alimentaria la principal causa en situaciones de urgencia. Esta condici\u00f3n se caracteriza por ser una reacci\u00f3n al\u00e9rgica intensa y potencialmente mortal que puede ocurrir de manera r\u00e1pida tras la exposici\u00f3n a un al\u00e9rgeno, como ciertos alimentos."}{"title": "ALERGIA:"}{"title": "DERMATITIS AT\u00d3PICA:Dermatitis at\u00f3pica es un tipo de eccema que comienza en la infancia, caracterizado por prurito intenso y remisiones y exacerbaciones, mediado por inmunidad celular e IgE."}{"title": "DERMATITIS DE CONTACTO:Dermatitis de contacto inducida por alimentos ocurre en manipuladores de alimentos crudos como pescado y marisco, causando reacciones cut\u00e1neas."}{"title": "RINOCONJUNTIVITIS:Rinoconjuntivitis es una reacci\u00f3n al\u00e9rgica que puede asociarse a otros s\u00edntomas at\u00f3picos, aunque raramente se presenta de forma aislada."}{"title": "ASMA:Asma es una manifestaci\u00f3n poco habitual de alergias alimentarias, que puede causar broncoespasmo agudo y est\u00e1 relacionada con al\u00e9rgenos alimentarios."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE HEINER:El s\u00edndrome de Heiner es una enfermedad rara que causa hemosiderosis pulmonar, t\u00edpicamente ocasionada por prote\u00ednas de la leche de vaca."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS AT\u00d3PICOS:Los s\u00edntomas at\u00f3picos son manifestaciones cl\u00ednicas que pueden incluir urticaria, asma y rinoconjuntivitis, asociados a alergias alimentarias."}{"title": "DIARREA OSM\u00d3TICA:La diarrea osm\u00f3tica es un tipo de diarrea que ocurre cuando hay una ingesta excesiva de ciertos az\u00facares, como el sorbitol."}{"title": "REACCIONES ADVERSAS ALIMENTARIAS:Las reacciones adversas alimentarias son respuestas no deseadas a la ingesta de alimentos, que pueden incluir intolerancias y alergias."}{"title": "PRICK TEST:Prueba cut\u00e1nea utilizada para diagnosticar alergias alimentarias mediadas por IgE mediante la aplicaci\u00f3n de un al\u00e9rgeno en la epidermis."}{"title": "RAST:Prueba in vitro que determina la existencia de IgE espec\u00edficas mediante radioinmunoensayo, \u00fatil para diagnosticar alergias alimentarias."}{"title": "DIETAS DE ELIMINACI\u00d3N:M\u00e9todo utilizado para identificar alimentos responsables de reacciones al\u00e9rgicas mediante la eliminaci\u00f3n de ciertos alimentos de la dieta."}{"title": "ALERGENO:ALERGENO es una sustancia que provoca reacciones al\u00e9rgicas en individuos sensibles. Puede incluir una variedad de alimentos, tales como leche, huevo, pescado y cacahuete. Los al\u00e9rgenos son el foco de las pruebas diagn\u00f3sticas para identificar alergias, ya que son responsables de desencadenar estas reacciones en personas que tienen sensibilidad a ellos. En resumen, un al\u00e9rgeno es cualquier sustancia capaz de causar una reacci\u00f3n al\u00e9rgica, siendo especialmente relevante en el contexto de las alergias alimentarias."}{"title": "DIETA DE ELIMINACION:La dieta de eliminaci\u00f3n es un enfoque utilizado para identificar alimentos que causan reacciones al\u00e9rgicas, donde se eliminan ciertos alimentos de la dieta durante un periodo de tiempo."}{"title": "PROVOCACION ORAL:La provocaci\u00f3n oral es una prueba que consiste en introducir cantidades progresivamente mayores de un alimento sospechoso para confirmar o descartar una alergia alimentaria."}{"title": "ESOFAGITIS EOSINOFILICA:La esofagitis eosinof\u00edlica es un trastorno mediado por c\u00e9lulas que puede causar reacciones al\u00e9rgicas y s\u00edntomas gastrointestinales, y se diagnostica a trav\u00e9s de biopsias."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS ESPECIFICOS:Los anticuerpos espec\u00edficos son prote\u00ednas producidas por el sistema inmunol\u00f3gico en respuesta a al\u00e9rgenos, y su presencia puede indicar una reacci\u00f3n al\u00e9rgica."}{"title": "ALERGOLOGOS:"}{"title": "TEST DE TOLERANCIA A LA LACTOSA:El test de tolerancia a la lactosa mide la respuesta gluc\u00e9mica tras la ingesti\u00f3n de lactosa, ayudando a diagnosticar la deficiencia de lactasa."}{"title": "BIOPSIA DE INTESTINO DELGADO:La biopsia de intestino delgado es un procedimiento invasivo que puede confirmar la intolerancia a la lactosa tras un test positivo, aunque no es com\u00fanmente utilizado."}{"title": "PCR DEL GEN DE LA LACTASA:La PCR del gen de la lactasa es una prueba gen\u00e9tica que ayuda a diferenciar entre hipolactasia primaria y secundaria, aunque no est\u00e1 disponible en la pr\u00e1ctica cl\u00ednica habitual."}{"title": "SENSIBILIZACI\u00d3N:La sensibilizaci\u00f3n es el proceso por el cual el sistema inmunol\u00f3gico se vuelve reactivo a ciertos al\u00e9rgenos, com\u00fanmente ocurriendo en los primeros a\u00f1os de vida."}{"title": "MEDICACI\u00d3N:La medicaci\u00f3n se refiere a los f\u00e1rmacos que pueden influir en el vaciado g\u00e1strico, lo que puede causar complicaciones como la diarrea en pacientes que reciben nutrici\u00f3n enteral. Adem\u00e1s, la medicaci\u00f3n incluye f\u00e1rmacos como la adrenalina, que se utilizan para neutralizar posibles reacciones severas durante las pruebas de alergias. En resumen, la medicaci\u00f3n abarca tanto los f\u00e1rmacos que afectan el sistema digestivo como aquellos que son esenciales para el manejo de reacciones al\u00e9rgicas."}{"title": "REACCI\u00d3N ANAFIL\u00c1CTICA:La reacci\u00f3n anafil\u00e1ctica es una respuesta severa y potencialmente mortal del sistema inmunol\u00f3gico a un al\u00e9rgeno, que puede ocurrir tras la ingesta de ciertos alimentos."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS GASTROINTESTINALES:Los trastornos gastrointestinales son condiciones que afectan el sistema digestivo y pueden ser tratados o diagnosticados mediante pruebas de intolerancia alimentaria."}{"title": "PROBLEMAS DERMATOL\u00d3GICOS:Los problemas dermatol\u00f3gicos son afecciones de la piel que pueden estar relacionadas con alergias o intolerancias alimentarias."}{"title": "SOCIETADES CIENT\u00cdFICAS DE ALERGOLOG\u00cdA:Las sociedades cient\u00edficas de alergolog\u00eda son organizaciones que estudian y promueven el conocimiento sobre alergias e intolerancias alimentarias."}{"title": "SOCIETADES CIENT\u00cdFICAS DE NUTRICI\u00d3N:Las sociedades cient\u00edficas de nutrici\u00f3n son organizaciones que investigan y educan sobre la relaci\u00f3n entre la alimentaci\u00f3n y la salud, incluyendo alergias e intolerancias."}{"title": "PERSONAL EXPERTO:"}{"title": "ALERGIA A LAS PROTE\u00cdNAS DE LA LECHE DE VACA:La alergia a las prote\u00ednas de la leche de vaca es un fen\u00f3meno com\u00fan en ni\u00f1os, con una prevalencia del 2-5% y puede causar reacciones severas si no se maneja adecuadamente."}{"title": "DIETAS EN SITUACIONES ESPECIALES:\"DIETAS EN SITUACIONES ESPECIALES\" is a comprehensive section that discusses dietary recommendations tailored for specific circumstances. It includes guidance for athletes, focusing on their unique nutritional needs to enhance performance and recovery. Additionally, this section addresses dietary requirements for individuals managing food allergies, emphasizing the importance of restricting allergens to ensure safety and health. Overall, \"DIETAS EN SITUACIONES ESPECIALES\" provides valuable insights into specialized diets that cater to both athletic performance and allergy management."}{"title": "INMUNOTERAPIAS:Tratamientos que buscan desensibilizar a los pacientes mediante la administraci\u00f3n controlada de al\u00e9rgenos para inducir tolerancia."}{"title": "REACCIONES ANAFIL\u00c1CTICAS:Las reacciones anafil\u00e1cticas son respuestas severas que pueden ocurrir con la ingesta de al\u00e9rgenos, como la leche, y requieren atenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica inmediata."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNAS DE LA LECHE:Las prote\u00ednas de la leche son los componentes que pueden causar alergias en los ni\u00f1os, siendo el al\u00e9rgeno m\u00e1s frecuente en esta poblaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "REGULAMENTO (UE) N.\u00ba 1169/2011:Reglamento del Parlamento Europeo y del Consejo sobre informaci\u00f3n alimentaria facilitada al consumidor, aplicable desde el 13 de diciembre de 2014."}{"title": "AEPNAA:AEPNAA is an organization dedicated to providing information and experiences concerning allergies and food intolerances. It serves as an association for patients, updating lists of foods and additives that may contain allergens. Additionally, AEPNAA functions as a forum for the exchange of information among individuals affected by these conditions, fostering a supportive community for those seeking guidance and resources related to allergies and food intolerances."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO ORAL:El tratamiento oral es un m\u00e9todo de inmunoterapia que permite instaurar mecanismos de tolerancia a nivel intestinal mediante la administraci\u00f3n del al\u00e9rgeno."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO NASAL:El tratamiento nasal es un m\u00e9todo de inmunoterapia que permite instaurar mecanismos de tolerancia a nivel bronquial."}{"title": "REACCIONES ADVERSAS:Las reacciones adversas son efectos no deseados que pueden ocurrir al exponer a un paciente sensibilizado al al\u00e9rgeno nocivo."}{"title": "PROCEDIMIENTOS TERAP\u00c9UTICOS:Los procedimientos terap\u00e9uticos correctivos son m\u00e9todos en estudio para tratar alergias alimentarias, incluyendo desensibilizaci\u00f3n y tolerancia."}{"title": "ALERGIA INFANTILLA FE:ALERGIA INFANTILLA FE is an organization dedicated to addressing childhood allergies and providing relevant resources."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNAS DE LA LECHE DE VACA:Cow's milk protein allergy is a common allergy in infants that can impact their nutrition and growth."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS HIDROLIZADAS:Hydrolyzed formulas contain proteins broken down into smaller peptides, making them easier to digest for allergic infants."}{"title": "DIETA BAJA EN HISTAMINA:La dieta baja en histamina se utiliza para tratar condiciones como urticaria y cefaleas cr\u00f3nicas, y se recomienda para personas con intolerancias alimentarias."}{"title": "ANTIHISTAM\u00cdNICO H1:El antihistam\u00ednico H1 es un medicamento que se recomienda para el tratamiento de alergias y se sugiere su uso durante 14 d\u00edas en el inicio del tratamiento diet\u00e9tico."}{"title": "SOCIETY OF PEDIATRIC GASTROENTEROLOGY, HEPATOLOGY AND NUTRITION:La Sociedad Europea de Gastroenterolog\u00eda, Hepatolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n Pedi\u00e1tricas (ESPGHAN) actualiza recomendaciones sobre la introducci\u00f3n de gluten en la dieta infantil."}{"title": "ACAD\u00c9MIA AMERICANA DE PEDIATR\u00cdA:The Academia Americana de Pediatr\u00eda (AAP) is an organization dedicated to pediatric health, providing essential guidelines and recommendations for various aspects of child care. Among its key contributions, the AAP offers advice on the introduction of solid foods for children at high risk of food allergies, ensuring that parents and caregivers are informed about best practices to promote health and safety. Additionally, since 2008, the AAP has also recommended vitamin D supplementation for children, highlighting its importance in maintaining optimal health during early development. Through these initiatives, the AAP plays a crucial role in guiding pediatric care and supporting the well-being of children."}{"title": "INHIBIDORES DE LA MONOAMINOXIDASA:Los inhibidores de la monoaminooxidasa (MAO) son medicamentos que pueden interactuar con la dieta baja en histamina y afectar la actividad de DAO."}{"title": "DIAMINOXIDASA:La diaminooxidasa (DAO) es una enzima que descompone la histamina en el cuerpo y su actividad puede ser insuficiente en personas con alergias alimentarias."}{"title": "DIETA BAJA EN FODMAP:"}{"title": "SOCIEDAD EUROPEA DE GASTROENTEROLOG\u00cdA, HEPATOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N PEDI\u00c1TRICAS:The European Society of Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition (ESPGHAN) is an organization that updates dietary recommendations for infants, particularly regarding gluten introduction."}{"title": "SICHERER:Sicherer is an author known for his work on the epidemiology of food allergies, contributing to the understanding of their prevalence."}{"title": "BOYCE:Boyce is an author who has contributed to guidelines for the diagnosis and management of food allergies in the United States."}{"title": "MADSEN:Madsen is an author who has provided an overview of the prevalence of food allergies in the medical literature."}{"title": "RONA:Rona is an author who has conducted a meta-analysis on the prevalence of food allergies."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3N BBVA:Fundaci\u00f3n BBVA is an organization that has published literature on allergic diseases, including food allergies."}{"title": "SEAIC:SEAIC is an organization involved in the study and management of allergic diseases, including food allergies."}{"title": "ALLEN:Allen is an author who has researched the association between vitamin D insufficiency and food allergies in infants."}{"title": "RODUIT:Roudiot is an author who has studied the relationship between food diversity in infancy and allergic diseases."}{"title": "ALONSO LEBRERO:"}{"title": "NIAID:The National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases (NIAID) is a part of the U.S. National Institutes of Health and is involved in research and guidelines related to food allergies."}{"title": "J ALLERGY CLIN IMMUNOL:The Journal of Allergy and Clinical Immunology is a peer-reviewed medical journal covering research in allergy and immunology."}{"title": "FOOD ALLERGY:Food Allergy refers to a medical condition characterized by an immune response triggered by the ingestion of certain foods. This abnormal reaction of the immune system can lead to a variety of allergic symptoms, which may vary in severity from mild to life-threatening."}{"title": "PEANUT ALLERGY:Peanut allergy is a specific type of food allergy that is common among children and can lead to severe allergic reactions."}{"title": "SAMSON HA:Sampson HA is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding and updates of food allergies."}{"title": "BOYCE JA:Boyce JA is a researcher involved in the guidelines for the diagnosis and management of food allergies."}{"title": "MULLINS RJ:Mullins RJ is a researcher who studied time trends in Australian hospital anaphylaxis admissions."}{"title": "HONG X:Hong X is a researcher who conducted a genome-wide association study related to peanut allergy in US children."}{"title": "DEPNER M:Depner M is a researcher involved in the study of food diversity and allergic diseases."}{"title": "FREI R:Frei R is a researcher who contributed to the study on food diversity and allergic diseases."}{"title": "SCHAUB B:Schaub B is a researcher who worked on the association between food diversity in infancy and allergic diseases."}{"title": "LOSS G:Loss G is a researcher involved in studies related to food allergies."}{"title": "GENUNEIT J:Genuneit J is a researcher who contributed to the study on food diversity and allergic diseases."}{"title": "PFEFFERLE P:Pfefferle P is a researcher involved in the study of food diversity and allergic diseases."}{"title": "HYV\u00c4RINEN A:Hyv\u00e4rinen A is a researcher who contributed to the study on food diversity and allergic diseases."}{"title": "KARVONEN AM:Karvonen AM is a researcher involved in the study of food diversity and allergic diseases."}{"title": "RIEDLER J:Riedler J is a researcher who contributed to the study on food diversity and allergic diseases."}{"title": "TANG MLK:Tang MLK is a researcher who studied environmental and demographic risk factors for egg allergy in infants."}{"title": "LOWE AJ:Lowe AJ is a researcher involved in the study of food allergies."}{"title": "MARTIN PE:Martin PE is a researcher who studied environmental and demographic risk factors for egg allergy in infants."}{"title": "ROBINSON MN:Robinson MN is a researcher involved in the study of food allergies."}{"title": "WAKE M:Wake M is a researcher who contributed to the study on food allergies."}{"title": "COLLIER F:Collier F is a researcher who contributed to the study on food allergy."}{"title": "NASELLI G:Naselli G is a researcher involved in the study of food allergy."}{"title": "SAFFERY R:Saffery R is a researcher who studied the relationship between cytokines and food allergy."}{"title": "PONSONBY A-L:Ponsonby A-L is a researcher who studied familial aggregation of food allergy."}{"title": "HARRISON LC:Harrison LC is a researcher involved in the study of food allergies."}{"title": "VUILLERMIN P:Vuillermin P is a researcher who contributed to the study on food allergies."}{"title": "HOLT PG:Holt PG is a researcher who studied viral infections and their relation to asthma and allergies."}{"title": "SLY PD:Sly PD is a researcher involved in the study of asthma pathogenesis."}{"title": "FEEHLEY T:Feehley T is a researcher who studied how commensal bacteria affect food allergy sensitization."}{"title": "ALLERGY:Allergy is a condition in which the immune system reacts abnormally to a substance, such as food."}{"title": "ANAPHYLAXIS:Anaphylaxis is a severe, potentially life-threatening allergic reaction that can occur in response to food allergies."}{"title": "FOOD DIVERSITY:Food diversity refers to the variety of foods consumed, which can impact health outcomes, including allergies."}{"title": "KOPLIN JJ:"}{"title": "NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF HEALTH:The National Institute of Health is a part of the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services and is responsible for biomedical and public health research."}{"title": "SAVAIANO D:Savaiano D is a researcher who has contributed to studies on lactose intolerance and its management."}{"title": "BIESIEKIERSKI JR:Biesiekierski JR is a researcher known for work on gluten sensitivity and its effects on gastrointestinal health."}{"title": "MARTINI MC:Martini MC is a researcher who has studied the effects of lactose consumption on intolerance symptoms."}{"title": "HALMOS EP:Halmos EP is a researcher who has investigated dietary interventions for irritable bowel syndrome."}{"title": "BROWN SR:Brown SR is a researcher who has studied the effects of coffee on colon function."}{"title": "LEA R:Lea R is a researcher known for work on food intolerance and its role in irritable bowel syndrome."}{"title": "WALKER R:Walker R is a researcher who has examined the significance of dietary components like monosodium glutamate."}{"title": "VERNIA P:Vernia P is a researcher who has investigated self-reported milk intolerance in irritable bowel syndrome."}{"title": "UNTERSMAYR E:Untersmayr E is a researcher who has studied the role of protein digestibility in food allergy outcomes."}{"title": "FLEISCHER DM:Fleischer DM is a researcher involved in studies on sublingual immunotherapy for peanut allergy."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF ALLERGY AND CLINICAL IMMUNOLOGY:"}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR PEDIATRIC GASTROENTEROLOGY, HEPATOLOGY, AND NUTRITION:The European Society for Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology, and Nutrition is a professional organization focused on the study and treatment of gastrointestinal and nutritional disorders in children."}{"title": "AMERICAN ACADEMY OF PEDIATRICS:The American Academy of Pediatrics is a professional association of pediatricians dedicated to the health and well-being of infants, children, adolescents, and young adults."}{"title": "TEST DE TOLERANCIA ORAL A LA GLUCOSA:El Test de Tolerancia Oral a la Glucosa (TTOG) es un procedimiento diagn\u00f3stico utilizado para detectar alteraciones en el metabolismo de los carbohidratos, que implica la administraci\u00f3n de una bebida con glucosa y la medici\u00f3n de los niveles de glucemia en diferentes intervalos de tiempo."}{"title": "GASTRECTOM\u00cdAS:Las gastrectom\u00edas son procedimientos quir\u00fargicos que implican la extirpaci\u00f3n parcial o total del est\u00f3mago, lo que puede afectar la interpretaci\u00f3n de pruebas como el TTOG."}{"title": "NATIONAL DIABETES DATA GROUP:The National Diabetes Data Group (NDDG) is an organization dedicated to providing guidelines and standards for the diagnosis and management of diabetes, including gestational diabetes. It has established criteria for the classification and diagnosis of diabetes mellitus and other categories of glucose intolerance, ensuring a comprehensive approach to understanding and addressing diabetes-related health issues."}{"title": "TTOG:The TTOG (test de tolerancia oral a la glucosa) is a medical test used to diagnose diabetes by measuring blood glucose levels after the ingestion of glucose."}{"title": "O'SULLIVAN TEST:The O'Sullivan test is a screening test for gestational diabetes that involves measuring blood glucose levels after consuming a glucose solution."}{"title": "GLUC\u00d3METRO:A gluc\u00f3metro is a device used for measuring blood glucose levels, particularly in patients with diabetes."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LISIS QU\u00cdMICO DE VAN DE KAMER:The an\u00e1lisis qu\u00edmico de Van de Kamer is a reference method used for the quantitative determination of fat in fecal samples, important for diagnosing conditions like esteatorrea."}{"title": "ACIDO ASCORBICO:A substance that can interfere with medical tests and is commonly known as Vitamin C."}{"title": "TOCOFEROL:TOCOFEROL is a substance commonly known as Vitamin E, which can interfere with medical tests. It is a form of vitamin E that is utilized as an antioxidant in dietary supplements."}{"title": "ADITIVOS ANTIOXIDANTES:Antioxidant additives that should be removed from the diet prior to certain medical tests to avoid false negatives."}{"title": "METODO DE OXIDACION DE CUERPOS FENOLICOS:A method used to detect blood in feces that requires dietary restrictions to avoid false positives."}{"title": "METODO DE INTERACCION ANTIGENO-ANTICUERPO:A method used to detect blood in feces that does not require dietary restrictions."}{"title": "ACIDO 5-HIDROXIINDOLACETICO:A metabolite of serotonin that is eliminated in urine and is used to diagnose carcinoid tumors."}{"title": "5-HIA:5-Hydroxyindoleacetic acid (5-HIA) is a metabolite of serotonin that is eliminated through urine and is used as a marker in diagnosing carcinoid tumors."}{"title": "VAMA:Vanilmandelic acid (VAMA) is a test used to diagnose tumors derived from chromaffin cells, such as pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas."}{"title": "DIETA ESPECIAL:A special diet is required before urine collection for tests to avoid false positives in the determination of metabolites like 5-HIA and VAMA."}{"title": "NEUROBLASTOMAS:Neuroblastomas are tumors that can arise from neuroblasts and are associated with catecholamine secretion, similar to pheochromocytomas."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS HOMOVAN\u00cdLICO Y VANILMAND\u00c9LICO:Homovanillic acid and vanilmandelic acid are metabolites of catecholamines used in the diagnosis of neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN YODO:Los alimentos ricos en yodo son aquellos que pueden afectar la eficacia de los tratamientos relacionados con el tiroides."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS CON M\u00cdNIMO RESIDUO:Los alimentos con m\u00ednimo residuo son aquellos que se deben consumir para facilitar estudios diagn\u00f3sticos del tubo digestivo."}{"title": "PET/TC:PET/TC is a non-invasive imaging diagnostic technique that uses a radiopharmaceutical to detect cancerous cells and evaluate glucose metabolism in various tissues."}{"title": "18FLUORODESOXYGLUCOSE:18fluorodesoxiglucosa (FDG) is a radiopharmaceutical used in PET scans, primarily taken up by cells with high glucose consumption, including cancer cells."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SOLUTIONS:Nutritional solutions are specialized supplements designed to ensure nutritional balance, particularly during dietary restrictions that may occur before medical tests. These solutions encompass a variety of formulations aimed at providing essential nutrients to patients, especially those who are unable to consume food orally. They play a crucial role in maintaining health and supporting recovery in individuals with specific dietary needs."}{"title": "CANCER CELLS:Cancer cells are cells that grow uncontrollably and are primarily targeted in PET scans for diagnosis and monitoring."}{"title": "CARNE FIBROSA:Carne fibrosa refers to fibrous meats that are typically avoided in diets leading up to medical tests to ensure clarity in imaging."}{"title": "FRUTAS Y VERDURAS FRESCAS:Frutas y verduras frescas are fresh fruits and vegetables that are generally restricted in diets before medical tests to avoid interference with results."}{"title": "FRUTAS DESSECADAS:Frutas dessecadas are dried fruits that are usually eliminated from diets prior to medical tests to ensure accurate imaging results."}{"title": "ZUMO DE CIRUELAS:Zumo de ciruelas is prune juice that is typically restricted in diets before medical tests to minimize interference with imaging results."}{"title": "CEREALES REFINADOS:Cereales refinados are refined grains that are allowed in diets before medical tests, as they are easier to digest."}{"title": "PATATAS PELADAS:Patatas peladas are peeled potatoes that are permitted in diets leading up to medical tests."}{"title": "CARNE TIERNA:Carne tierna refers to tender meat that is allowed in diets before medical tests."}{"title": "AGUA NO SABORIZADA:Agua no saborizada is plain water that is the only liquid permitted during the fasting period before a PET/TC scan."}{"title": "EJERCICIO F\u00cdSICO INTENSO:Se aconseja evitar el ejercicio f\u00edsico intenso 24 horas antes de la prueba para no afectar los resultados."}{"title": "PRUEBAS DIAGN\u00d3STICAS:Procedimientos m\u00e9dicos que requieren ayuno previo para obtener resultados precisos."}{"title": "RADIOTRAZADOR:Sustancia utilizada en pruebas m\u00e9dicas que puede ser afectada por la ingesta de alimentos y glucosa."}{"title": "CARPENTER MW:Carpenter MW is a researcher known for establishing criteria for screening tests for gestational diabetes."}{"title": "BULL\u00d3 I BONET M:Bull\u00f3 i Bonet M is an author who contributed to the quantification of fats in feces in clinical nutrition literature."}{"title": "\u00d6BERG KE:\u00d6berg KE is a researcher who has written about carcinoid tumors and related disorders in endocrinology literature."}{"title": "GESTATIONAL DIABETES:Gestational diabetes is a form of diabetes that occurs during pregnancy and is addressed in the screening criteria established by Carpenter MW."}{"title": "BARCELONA:Barcelona is a city in Spain renowned for its rich cultural heritage. It serves as a significant publishing location for Ediciones Doyma, which is known for producing various publications on medical ethics and nutrition. This dual role highlights Barcelona's importance not only as a cultural hub but also as a center for important academic and professional literature."}{"title": "EDICIONES DOYMA:Ediciones Doyma is a publishing company based in Barcelona, known for its medical and clinical literature."}{"title": "LIPPINCOTT-RAVEN:Lippincott-Raven is a publishing company that specializes in medical and clinical texts, with publications based in Philadelphia."}{"title": "WJG:WJG is a medical journal that publishes research and reviews in the field of gastroenterology."}{"title": "AJR:AJR is a journal that publishes articles related to radiology and medical imaging."}{"title": "HORMONE SYNTHESIS:Hormone synthesis, particularly thyroid iodine metabolism, is a critical process in endocrinology, discussed in medical texts."}{"title": "BOWEL PREPARATION:Bowel preparation is a medical procedure necessary before colonoscopy, involving dietary restrictions and cleansing protocols."}{"title": "ENHANCED RECOVERY AFTER SURGERY (ERAS):ERAS is a set of guidelines aimed at improving recovery after surgical procedures, particularly in colonic and pancreatic surgeries."}{"title": "COMPLEJO ASISTENCIAL:The Complejo Asistencial in Le\u00f3n is a healthcare institution where various medical professionals work, including those specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "JOINT COMMISSION ON ACCREDITATION OF HEALTHCARE ORGANIZATIONS:The Joint Commission on Accreditation of Healthcare Organizations (JCAHO) is an organization dedicated to establishing standards for healthcare quality and accreditation in the United States. It serves as an external agent that verifies whether healthcare organizations comply with specific quality standards, ensuring that they provide safe and effective care to patients."}{"title": "INTERACCIONES:INTERACCIONES refers to the interactions between drugs and diet, as well as between drugs and nutrients, which are significant in clinical settings and can affect treatment outcomes. These interactions are particularly relevant in nutritional therapy and must be considered to avoid adverse effects. Understanding these interacciones is crucial for optimizing treatment efficacy and ensuring patient safety."}{"title": "INTERACCI\u00d3N FARMACO-NUTRIENTE:La interacci\u00f3n f\u00e1rmaco-nutriente se refiere a c\u00f3mo los f\u00e1rmacos y los nutrientes pueden influenciarse mutuamente en su eficacia y absorci\u00f3n."}{"title": "AMOXICILINA:La amoxicilina es un antibi\u00f3tico que puede tener su biodisponibilidad afectada por la fibra de la dieta."}{"title": "PARACETAMOL:Paracetamol is a widely used analgesic and antipyretic medication that is effective in treating mild to moderate pain and reducing fever. Its absorption can be influenced by dietary components, which may affect its overall efficacy."}{"title": "LEVODOPA:Levodopa is a medication primarily used in the treatment of Parkinson's disease. It is known to interact with various substances, including iron, which can chelate the drug, potentially affecting its efficacy. Additionally, levodopa's metabolism can be influenced by vitamin B6, indicating a possible interaction that may alter its therapeutic effects. The absorption of levodopa is also significantly impacted by dietary factors, particularly the presence of food, with high-protein meals being particularly detrimental to its absorption. Overall, these interactions highlight the importance of considering dietary and nutritional factors when administering levodopa to patients with Parkinson's disease."}{"title": "ZUMOS:Los zumos son bebidas que pueden tener un pH \u00e1cido y afectar la absorci\u00f3n de ciertos f\u00e1rmacos."}{"title": "INTERACCI\u00d3N MEDICAMENTO-NUTRIENTE:La interacci\u00f3n medicamento-nutriente se refiere a c\u00f3mo los medicamentos pueden afectar la utilizaci\u00f3n de los nutrientes y el estado nutricional."}{"title": "INTERACCI\u00d3N ALIMENTO-MEDICAMENTO:"}{"title": "ETILSUCINATO:Etilsuccinato is a compound that is less susceptible to acidic pH, leading to more complete absorption compared to other compounds."}{"title": "ESTOLATO:Estolato is a compound that is less susceptible to acidic pH, leading to more complete absorption compared to other compounds."}{"title": "ESTEARATO:Estearato is a compound that is more susceptible to acidic pH, affecting its absorption."}{"title": "GRISEOFULVINA:Griseofulvina is a medication known for its ability to cause abnormal taste sensations. It is characterized as liposoluble, meaning it dissolves in fats, and its absorption in the body is enhanced by the presence of bile salts."}{"title": "HALOFANTRINA:Halofantrina is a medication that is liposoluble and its absorption is facilitated by bile salts."}{"title": "FURANOCUMARINAS:Furanocoumarins are compounds found in grapefruit juice that can inhibit the CYP3A4 enzyme, affecting drug metabolism."}{"title": "INTERACCIONES FARMACOCIN\u00c9TICAS:Interacciones farmacocin\u00e9ticas are interactions that alter the pharmacokinetics of a drug, affecting its absorption, distribution, metabolism, and excretion."}{"title": "MOTILIDAD:Motilidad refers to the physiological movement within the gastrointestinal tract that can affect drug absorption."}{"title": "SECRECIONES GASTROINTESTINALES:Secreciones gastrointestinales are bodily fluids produced in the gastrointestinal tract that play a crucial role in the dissolution and absorption of medications. These secretions contain various electrolytes and minerals, which are essential for the proper functioning of the digestive system."}{"title": "PH:pH is a critical measure that influences various biological and chemical processes, particularly in the context of clinical nutrition and pharmacology. It affects the solubility of proteins in clinical nutrition products, thereby impacting their stability and effectiveness. Additionally, pH refers to the acidity or alkalinity of the gastrointestinal environment, which plays a significant role in drug absorption. Understanding pH is essential for optimizing both nutritional products and medication efficacy."}{"title": "F\u00c1RMACO:F\u00e1rmaco refers to the medication used in the treatment of conditions such as Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). In this context, tolvapt\u00e1n is specifically mentioned as the medication utilized for this purpose."}{"title": "ISONIAZIDA:Isoniazida is a medication that is primarily used in the treatment of tuberculosis. It is important for patients to be aware that Isoniazida can cause adverse reactions when ingested with foods containing histamine, which may lead to symptoms such as facial flushing and severe headache. To enhance the absorption of the medication, it is recommended that Isoniazida be taken on an empty stomach."}{"title": "ZIDOVUDINA:Zidovudina is an antiretroviral medication whose absorption can be significantly reduced by high-fat foods."}{"title": "DIETAS RICAS EN VITAMINA K:Diets high in vitamin K can antagonize the effects of anticoagulants like warfarina."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN HISTAMINA:Foods high in histamine can provoke hypertensive crises in patients taking monoamine oxidase inhibitors."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN GRASA:High-fat foods can reduce the absorption of certain antiretroviral medications by up to 50%."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN AJO:"}{"title": "MEPROBAMATO:Meprobamato is a basic medication that can have increased absorption when the pH of the stomach is raised by food."}{"title": "DICUMARINICOS:Dicumar\u00ednicos are anticoagulant medications that can have increased absorption when food slows gastric emptying."}{"title": "SAL DE LITIO:Sal de litio is a medication whose renal excretion can be influenced by dietary sodium intake."}{"title": "ACIDO ACETILSALICILICO:"}{"title": "BRASSICA:Brassica is a genus of vegetables including cabbage, cauliflower, and kale, known for their enzymatic induction properties affecting drug metabolism."}{"title": "AVOCADO:Avocado is a fruit that decreases the efficacy of oral anticoagulants due to its high fat content."}{"title": "GRAPEFRUIT JUICE:Grapefruit juice contains flavonoids that inhibit the metabolism of several drugs by affecting the CYP3A4 enzyme."}{"title": "ONIONS:Onions are rich in flavonoids and can potentiate the effects of anticoagulants due to their fibrinolytic activity."}{"title": "LICORICE:Licorice can antagonize the effects of antihypertensives and increase the risk of toxicity with digitalis due to sodium retention and hypokalemia."}{"title": "SOY:Soy contains phytoestrogens that can antagonize the antiestrogenic action of tamoxifen."}{"title": "PHENYTOIN:Phenytoin is a medication whose metabolism can be reduced by acute alcohol consumption."}{"title": "ANTIDEPRESSANTS:Antidepressants, particularly tricyclics, can have enhanced depressant effects on the central nervous system when combined with alcohol."}{"title": "CLORANFENICOL:Chloramphenicol is a medication that can have enhanced hepatotoxic effects when taken with alcohol."}{"title": "BETA-BLOCKERS:Beta-blockers can have their hypotensive effects potentiated by alcohol consumption."}{"title": "ANTICOAGULANTS:"}{"title": "ANTIHYPERTENSIVES:"}{"title": "TAMOXIFEN:"}{"title": "ANTIPIRINA:Antipirina is a medication whose metabolism can be influenced by dietary factors, particularly by enzymatic inducers."}{"title": "BARBITURICOS:Barbituricos are medications whose elimination can be enhanced by dietary alkalinization."}{"title": "QUININA:Quinina is a medication whose elimination can be affected by dietary acidification."}{"title": "DIGITALICOS:Digitalicos are medications that can have their effects antagonized by licorice, leading to toxicity risks."}{"title": "TERFENADINA:Terfenadina is a drug whose metabolism can be inhibited by grapefruit juice, leading to increased levels."}{"title": "ASTEMIZOL:Astemizol is a medication that can have its metabolism affected by grapefruit juice, increasing its levels."}{"title": "CARBAMAZEPINA:Carbamazepina is a medication that is known to have its metabolism influenced by alcohol, which can result in altered effects when both substances are present. To minimize gastrointestinal discomfort, it is recommended that Carbamazepina be taken with meals."}{"title": "QUINIDINA:Quinidina is a medication that can have its effects altered by alcohol consumption."}{"title": "MACROLIDOS:Macrolidos are antibiotics that can have their hepatotoxic effects enhanced by alcohol."}{"title": "G\u00d3MEZ ENTERR\u00cdA:G\u00f3mez Enterr\u00eda is referenced as a source for information regarding the effects of certain medications and their interactions."}{"title": "BEZAFIBRATO:Bezafibrato is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "ALMAGATO:Almagato is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "AMINOFILINA:Aminofilina is a medication that should be taken on an empty stomach to increase absorption."}{"title": "MALGADRATO:Malgadrato is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "ATENOLOL:Atenolol is a medication that should be taken on an empty stomach to increase absorption."}{"title": "CARBOCISTE\u00cdNA:Carbociste\u00edna is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "ALOPURINOL:Alopurinol is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "CAPTOPRIL:Captopril is a medication that should be taken on an empty stomach to increase absorption."}{"title": "CEFUROXIMA:Cefuroxima is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "HIDR\u00d3XIDO DE ALUMINIO:Hidr\u00f3xido de aluminio is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "CEFACLOR:Cefaclor is a medication that should be taken on an empty stomach to increase absorption."}{"title": "AMITRIPTILINA:Amitriptilina is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "CLOXACILINA:Cloxacilina is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "AZATIAPRINA:Azatioprina is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "COTRIMOXAZOL:Cotrimoxazol is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "DIAZEPAM:Diazepam is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "BROMOCRIPTINA:Bromocriptina is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "DIPIRIDAMOL:Dipiridamol is a medication that should be taken on an empty stomach to increase absorption."}{"title": "DILTIAZEM:Diltiazem is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "DOXICICLINA:Doxiciclina is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "F\u00d3LICO:F\u00d3LICO refers to Folic Acid, also known as Vitamin B9, which is a water-soluble vitamin essential for DNA synthesis and repair. It plays a critical role during periods of rapid growth, making it particularly important for pregnant women and individuals in developmental stages. Additionally, F\u00f3lico is a medication that is recommended to be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. This dual significance highlights F\u00d3LICO's importance both as a vital nutrient and as a therapeutic agent."}{"title": "ESPIROLACTONA:Espirolactona is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "FENITO\u00cdNA:Fenito\u00edna is an anticonvulsant medication that requires careful monitoring when administered with enteral nutrition due to its narrow therapeutic range. It is important to note that the plasma levels of Fenito\u00edna can be significantly reduced when given alongside enteral nutrition, which necessitates close observation of its effectiveness. To minimize gastrointestinal discomfort, it is recommended that Fenito\u00edna be taken with meals. Additionally, Fenito\u00edna can impact vitamin D metabolism, which is an important consideration in its use."}{"title": "DICLOFENACO:Diclofenaco is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "FLUTAMIDA:Flutamida is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "DIFENHIDRAMINA:Difenhidramina is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "GANCICLOVIR:Ganciclovir is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "ETAMBUTOL:Etambutol is a medication that should be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "G\u00d3ME(\"ENTITY\":"}{"title": "INTERFER\u00d3N ALFA:Interfer\u00f3n alfa is a medication that can decrease appetite."}{"title": "CARBONATO DE LITIO:Carbonato de litio is a medication that can cause abnormal taste sensations."}{"title": "MERCAPTOPURINA:Mercaptopurina is a medication used in the treatment of certain types of cancer and autoimmune diseases."}{"title": "INDOMETACINA:Indometacina is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) used to treat pain and inflammation."}{"title": "METOPROLOL:Metoprolol is a beta-blocker used to treat high blood pressure and heart-related conditions."}{"title": "LISURIDA:Lisurida is a medication used to treat Parkinson's disease and other conditions related to dopamine deficiency."}{"title": "MORFINA:Morfina is a powerful opioid pain medication used to treat severe pain."}{"title": "METAMIZOL:Metamizol is a pain reliever and antipyretic used to treat pain and fever."}{"title": "NIMODIPINO:Nimodipino is a calcium channel blocker used to prevent brain damage following a subarachnoid hemorrhage."}{"title": "METILDOPA:Metildopa is an antihypertensive medication used to treat high blood pressure, especially in pregnancy."}{"title": "NORFLOXACINO:Norfloxacino is an antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections, particularly urinary tract infections."}{"title": "NITROFURANTO\u00cdNA:Nitrofuranto\u00edna is an antibiotic used to treat urinary tract infections."}{"title": "METILPREDNISOLONA:Metilprednisolona is a corticosteroid used to treat inflammation and autoimmune conditions."}{"title": "PROPRANOLOL:Propranolol is a beta-blocker used to treat high blood pressure, anxiety, and other conditions."}{"title": "NAPROXENO:Naproxeno is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) used to relieve pain and inflammation."}{"title": "PIRIZINAMIDA:Pirizinamida is an antibiotic used in the treatment of tuberculosis."}{"title": "RANITIDINA:Ranitidina is a medication that is primarily used to reduce stomach acid and treat conditions such as gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD). In exceptional cases, it can also be included in parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "RETINOL:Retinol is a form of vitamin A that plays a significant role in both dietary intake and skincare. It is associated with specific dietary recommendations for consumption, highlighting its importance in nutrition. Additionally, retinol is widely utilized in skincare products and dietary supplements, underscoring its versatility and effectiveness in promoting skin health and overall well-being."}{"title": "\u00c1C. PIPEM\u00cdDICO:\u00c1cido pipem\u00eddico is an antibiotic used to treat urinary tract infections."}{"title": "PIROXICAM:Piroxicam is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) used to relieve pain and inflammation."}{"title": "TRIAMTERENO:Triamtereno is a potassium-sparing diuretic used to treat high blood pressure and fluid retention."}{"title": "TEOFILINA:Teofilina is a medication primarily used to treat respiratory diseases, including asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). Its therapeutic action can be influenced by dietary factors, as it is metabolized more quickly when a diet rich in proteins is consumed. This interaction may affect the effectiveness of the medication in managing respiratory conditions."}{"title": "VERAPAMILO RETARD:Verapamilo retard is a calcium channel blocker used to treat high blood pressure and heart conditions."}{"title": "TETRACICLINA:Tetraciclina is an antibiotic used to treat a variety of bacterial infections."}{"title": "\u00c1C. VALPROICO:\u00c1cido valproico is a medication used to treat epilepsy and bipolar disorder."}{"title": "ZIDOVIDINA:Zidovudina is an antiretroviral medication used to treat HIV/AIDS."}{"title": "TUNEU7:Tuneu7 is the author or source of the modified document discussing drug interactions and dietary effects."}{"title": "TEMA 44:Tema 44 refers to the specific topic of interaction between diet and drugs as discussed in the document."}{"title": "EFECTO MASA:Efecto masa refers to the phenomenon where certain medications induce a feeling of fullness or satiety."}{"title": "ESTOMATITIS:Estomatitis refers to inflammation of the mucous membrane in the mouth, which can be a side effect of certain medications."}{"title": "DEFICIENCIA:Deficiencia refers to the lack of essential nutrients in the body, which can result from interactions with medications."}{"title": "EFECTO TOXICO:Efecto t\u00f3xico refers to the harmful effects that certain medications can have on the body, particularly on the gastrointestinal mucosa."}{"title": "ANTIVITAMINAS:Antivitaminas refers to substances that interfere with the action of vitamins in the body, often due to medication interactions."}{"title": "DIUR\u00c9TICOS DE ASA:Diur\u00e9ticos de asa are a class of diuretics that can lead to the loss of essential minerals."}{"title": "FITOESTR\u00d3GENOS:Fitoestr\u00f3genos are plant-derived compounds that can mimic estrogen and interact with certain medications."}{"title": "IPRIFLAVONA:Ipriflavona is a compound that acts as an inhibitor of certain enzymes and can interact with medications.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "DIFENILHIDANTOINA:Difenilhidanto\u00edna is a medication that can show signs of toxicity at therapeutic doses, particularly in cases of hipoalbuminemia."}{"title": "CUMAR\u00cdNICOS:Cumar\u00ednicos are a class of medications that can also exhibit toxicity at therapeutic doses, influenced by factors such as hipoalbuminemia."}{"title": "SOCIETY ESPA\u00d1OLA DE NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL Y PARENTERAL:"}{"title": "DIETA RICA EN PROTE\u00cdNAS:A high-protein diet can lead to increased production of cytochrome P450 enzymes, affecting the metabolism of certain medications like teofilina."}{"title": "DIETA RICA EN GRASAS:A high-fat diet can displace drugs bound to plasma proteins, potentially altering their effectiveness and absorption."}{"title": "DIETAS HIPOCAL\u00d3RICAS:Hypocaloric diets can increase protein catabolism, affecting the quantity and activity of enzymes responsible for drug metabolism."}{"title": "GASTROINTESTINAL TRACT:The gastrointestinal tract is the organ system that is affected by medications and can influence the tolerance of enteral nutrition."}{"title": "AEROFAGIA:Aerofagia is a condition that can be caused by high sorbitol content in liquid formulations, affecting tolerance to enteral nutrition."}{"title": "BEZOARES ESOF\u00c1GICOS:Bezoares esof\u00e1gicos are blockages that can occur in the esophagus due to interactions between medications and enteral nutrition."}{"title": "ANTIHISTAM\u00cdNICOS:Antihistam\u00ednicos are medications that can inhibit gastric motility."}{"title": "FENOTIACINAS:Fenotiacinas are medications that can inhibit gastric motility."}{"title": "ANTIPARKINSONIANOS:Antiparkinsonianos are medications that can inhibit gastric motility."}{"title": "INTERACCI\u00d3N FARMACODIN\u00c1MICA:Interacci\u00f3n farmacodin\u00e1mica occurs when there are alterations in the pharmacological action of a drug or the nutritional properties of a preparation without changes in pharmacokinetics."}{"title": "ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N CONJUNTA:Administraci\u00f3n conjunta refers to the simultaneous administration of drugs and enteral nutrition, which can lead to interactions affecting drug efficacy."}{"title": "PREVENCI\u00d3N DE INTERACCIONES:Prevenci\u00f3n de interacciones involves recommendations for administering medications to minimize interactions with enteral nutrition."}{"title": "FORMAS FARMAC\u00c9UTICAS:Formas farmac\u00e9uticas refer to the various pharmaceutical forms of medications that can affect their absorption and efficacy when administered with enteral nutrition."}{"title": "CUBIERTA ENTERICA:Cubierta ent\u00e9rica is a type of pharmaceutical form designed to protect the active ingredient from degradation in the stomach."}{"title": "LIBERACI\u00d3N RETARDADA:Liberaci\u00f3n retardada refers to pharmaceutical forms that release the active ingredient slowly over time, which can be affected by crushing the medication."}{"title": "ABSORCI\u00d3N SUBLINGUAL:Absorci\u00f3n sublingual refers to the absorption of medications directly into the bloodstream through the tissues under the tongue, which can be altered by enteral nutrition."}{"title": "COMPRIMIDOS EFERVESCENTES:Comprimidos efervescentes are effervescent tablets that can be affected by the administration route and formulation when given with enteral nutrition."}{"title": "C\u00c1PSULAS:C\u00e1psulas are a form of medication that can contain granules with enteric coating, which should not be crushed to maintain their efficacy."}{"title": "ZUMO \u00c1CIDO DE FRUTAS:Zumo \u00e1cido de frutas is a liquid that can be used to administer certain medications through a feeding tube without compromising their integrity.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "THOMSON14:Thomson14 is referenced as a source for guidelines on the administration of medications via enteral feeding tubes."}{"title": "DICUMAR\u00cdNICOS:Dicumar\u00ednicos are anticoagulant medications that need special precautions when administered with enteral nutrition."}{"title": "FORMULACIONES:Las formulaciones l\u00edquidas son preparaciones que pueden contener nutrientes y f\u00e1rmacos, y su composici\u00f3n puede influir en las interacciones que ocurren en el tracto gastrointestinal."}{"title": "SORBITO:"}{"title": "AGENCIA ESPA\u00d1OLA DE PROTECCI\u00d3N DE LA SALUD EN EL DEPORTE:The Agency for the Protection of Health in Sports (AEPSAD) is responsible for promoting health and nutrition in sports in Spain."}{"title": "NIEVES PALACIOS GIL DE ANTU\u00d1ANO:Nieves Palacios Gil de Antu\u00f1ano is the Head of the Medicine, Endocrinology, and Nutrition Service at AEPSAD."}{"title": "FERNANDO GARC\u00cdA P\u00c9REZ-SEVILLANO:Fernando Garc\u00eda P\u00e9rez-Sevillano is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition based in Sevilla."}{"title": "HIP\u00d3CRATES:Hippocrates was an ancient Greek physician who emphasized the importance of diet and exercise for health."}{"title": "DIETA SANA:A healthy diet is a key component of maintaining good health and is emphasized in the context of physical activity."}{"title": "DEPORTISTA:A \"DEPORTISTA\" is an individual who actively engages in sports or physical exercise, with a strong emphasis on enhancing performance through proper training and nutrition. This athlete not only participates in physical activities but also adheres to specific dietary guidelines and hydration practices to achieve optimal results. The deportista is dedicated to improving their performance and overall health by following structured and regulated exercise routines. Their commitment to both physical activity and nutritional needs is essential for maximizing their athletic capabilities."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N EQUILIBRADA:La alimentaci\u00f3n equilibrada es un plan nutricional que satisface los requerimientos de energ\u00eda necesarios para sostener el programa de competici\u00f3n y rendir a alto nivel."}{"title": "ENTRENAMIENTO DEPORTIVO:El entrenamiento deportivo es la pr\u00e1ctica sistem\u00e1tica, regular y progresiva del ejercicio f\u00edsico para mejorar el rendimiento deportivo."}{"title": "SISTEMAS ENERG\u00c9TICOS:Los sistemas energ\u00e9ticos son las v\u00edas utilizadas por el m\u00fasculo esquel\u00e9tico para cubrir sus demandas energ\u00e9ticas durante el ejercicio."}{"title": "RENDIMIENTO:El rendimiento se refiere a la capacidad de un deportista para ejecutar su deporte de manera efectiva, influenciado por la nutrici\u00f3n y el entrenamiento."}{"title": "DEPORTISTAS:Deportistas refers to athletes who actively engage in physical activities and sports, focusing on improving their performance through various nutritional and physical aids. They are the primary subjects of the nutritional guidelines and recommendations discussed in the document. These individuals face health and performance challenges related to their available energy and are particularly susceptible to iron deficiency. As such, specific nutritional guidelines are essential for enhancing their performance and recovery."}{"title": "COMPETICIONES:Las competiciones son eventos deportivos donde los deportistas participan y pueden beneficiarse de una adecuada ingesta de hidratos de carbono."}{"title": "DIETA DEL DEPORTISTA:La dieta del deportista debe incluir una alta ingesta de hidratos de carbono para optimizar el rendimiento f\u00edsico."}{"title": "RESERVAS DE GLUC\u00d3GENO:Las reservas de gluc\u00f3geno son la cantidad de gluc\u00f3geno almacenado en los m\u00fasculos y el h\u00edgado, crucial para el rendimiento deportivo."}{"title": "CLOSE ET AL:Close et al (2015) proposed practical guidelines for carbohydrate intake to optimize training loads with reduced muscle glycogen levels"}{"title": "CARGA DE ENTRENAMIENTO:Refers to the training load or intensity that an athlete undergoes during their training sessions"}{"title": "INGESTA DE HIDRATOS DE CARBONO:The process of consuming carbohydrates before, during, and after exercise to enhance performance"}{"title": "ALTA INTENSIDAD:Refers to high-intensity training sessions that require specific carbohydrate intake for optimal performance"}{"title": "BAJA INTENSIDAD:Refers to low-intensity training sessions that have different carbohydrate intake requirements"}{"title": "PRODUCTOS PARA DEPORTISTAS:Los productos para deportistas incluyen una variedad de alimentos y bebidas dise\u00f1ados para proporcionar carbohidratos de f\u00e1cil consumo durante el ejercicio."}{"title": "GLUC\u00d3GENO MUSCULAR:El gluc\u00f3geno muscular es la forma en que se almacena la glucosa en los m\u00fasculos, y es crucial para el rendimiento durante el ejercicio."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTESIS DE GLUC\u00d3GENO:La s\u00edntesis de gluc\u00f3geno es el proceso mediante el cual el cuerpo repone el gluc\u00f3geno muscular y hep\u00e1tico despu\u00e9s del ejercicio, crucial para la recuperaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "TRANSPORTADORES DE GLUCOSA:Los transportadores de glucosa son prote\u00ednas que facilitan la absorci\u00f3n de glucosa en el cuerpo, esenciales para el metabolismo de los carbohidratos."}{"title": "EJERCICIO DE ULTRARESISTENCIA:El ejercicio de ultrarresistencia se refiere a actividades f\u00edsicas que duran m\u00e1s de 2,5-3 horas, donde se requiere una ingesta elevada de carbohidratos para mantener el rendimiento."}{"title": "\u00cdNDICE GLUC\u00c9MICO:\u00cdNDICE GLUC\u00c9MICO is a measure that indicates how quickly a carbohydrate-containing food raises blood glucose levels. It classifies foods based on their impact on blood glucose levels, which is particularly important for the selection of carbohydrates after exercise."}{"title": "ALMACENAMIENTO DE GLUC\u00d3GENO:The process of glycogen storage is vital for athletes to maintain energy levels during prolonged physical activities."}{"title": "ADAPTACI\u00d3N:Adaptation refers to the physiological changes that occur in the body in response to training, improving performance and efficiency in energy use."}{"title": "STUART M. PHILLIPS:Stuart M. Phillips is a researcher who suggests optimal protein intake for muscle synthesis and hypertrophy."}{"title": "EJERCICIO DE FUERZA:Strength training exercises that promote muscle growth and increase protein synthesis."}{"title": "EJERCICIO DE RESISTENCIA:\"EJERCICIO DE RESISTENCIA\" refers to endurance exercises that are crucial for muscle development. These activities not only enhance physical performance but also consistently increase the protein requirements for individuals, particularly athletes. This type of exercise plays a fundamental role in promoting muscle growth and overall physical fitness."}{"title": "ENTRENAMIENTO DE FUERZA:El entrenamiento de fuerza es un tipo de ejercicio que, cuando se asocia con un incremento en la ingesta de prote\u00ednas, puede conducir a un aumento del desarrollo muscular."}{"title": "TR\u00cdADA DE LA MUJER DEPORTISTA:La tr\u00edada de la mujer deportista es un s\u00edndrome que incluye des\u00f3rdenes alimentarios, amenorrea y osteoporosis, afectando la salud de las deportistas."}{"title": "TERMORREGULACI\u00d3N:La termorregulaci\u00f3n es el proceso que el cuerpo utiliza para disipar el calor acumulado durante el ejercicio, crucial para el rendimiento deportivo."}{"title": "MENSTRUACI\u00d3N:La menstruaci\u00f3n puede aumentar la p\u00e9rdida de hierro en algunas mujeres, contribuyendo a la deficiencia de hierro en deportistas."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N INADECUADA:La nutrici\u00f3n inadecuada, combinada con ejercicio intenso, puede llevar a un d\u00e9ficit energ\u00e9tico en deportistas."}{"title": "SUDOR:El sudor es un l\u00edquido producido por las gl\u00e1ndulas sudor\u00edparas que ayuda a regular la temperatura corporal durante el ejercicio."}{"title": "CALAMBRES:Los calambres son contracciones musculares involuntarias que pueden ocurrir como resultado de la deshidrataci\u00f3n y el desequilibrio electrol\u00edtico."}{"title": "CONSCIENCIA:La consciencia se refiere al estado de alerta y percepci\u00f3n de una persona, que puede verse afectado por la deshidrataci\u00f3n."}{"title": "ESTRATEGIA DE HIDRATACI\u00d3N:Una estrategia de hidrataci\u00f3n es un plan dise\u00f1ado para asegurar que un deportista mantenga un nivel adecuado de l\u00edquidos durante el ejercicio."}{"title": "RADIACI\u00d3N SOLAR:La radiaci\u00f3n solar es la energ\u00eda emitida por el sol, que puede afectar la temperatura corporal y la necesidad de hidrataci\u00f3n durante el ejercicio."}{"title": "HUMEDAD:La humedad es la cantidad de vapor de agua en el aire, que puede afectar la hidrataci\u00f3n y el rendimiento de los deportistas durante el ejercicio."}{"title": "TEMPERATURA:TEMPERATURA refers to the degree of heat in the environment, which can significantly influence various factors, including the hydration needs of athletes during exercise. Additionally, TEMPERATURA encompasses the temperature conditions under which clinical nutrition products are processed, which is crucial for maintaining the stability and solubility of proteins and other ingredients in clinical nutrition formulations. Therefore, temperature is a critical element that affects both physical performance in sports and the quality of nutritional products."}{"title": "COMIT\u00c9 CIENT\u00cdFICO EN ALIMENTACI\u00d3N HUMANA:The Scientific Committee on Human Nutrition (CCAH) of the European Union provides guidelines on the composition of foods and beverages for energy expenditure during intense muscular effort, especially for athletes."}{"title": "BEBIDAS DEPORTIVAS:BEBIDAS DEPORTIVAS, or sports drinks, are specially designed beverages intended for athletes to maintain proper hydroelectrolytic balance during physical activity. These drinks provide essential hydration and energy, supporting athletes in their performance and endurance while engaging in sports or exercise."}{"title": "GASTO DE GLUC\u00d3GENO MUSCULAR:Muscle glycogen expenditure refers to the use of stored carbohydrates in muscles during physical activity, which can be influenced by hydration and carbohydrate intake."}{"title": "CCAH:The Comisi\u00f3n de Alimentaci\u00f3n Humana (CCAH) is an organization dedicated to promoting health and nutrition, particularly in the context of athletic performance. CCAH advocates for specific guidelines concerning isotonic beverages, focusing on their osmolality to ensure optimal hydration and energy replenishment for athletes. Additionally, the organization has drafted a comprehensive report on the composition of foods and beverages designed to meet the energy expenditure needs of individuals engaged in intense muscular efforts, emphasizing the importance of proper nutrition in athletic training and performance."}{"title": "FEDERACI\u00d3N ESPA\u00d1OLA DE MEDICINA DEL DEPORTE:The Federaci\u00f3n Espa\u00f1ola de Medicina del Deporte is a group that published a consensus document on nutrition in 2008, endorsing specific beverage compositions for athletes."}{"title": "ERGOGENIA:Ergogenia refers to methods and techniques aimed at enhancing physical and mental performance in sports."}{"title": "TAURINA:TAURINA, also known as taurine, is a sulfur-containing amino acid that plays a crucial role in various physiological functions. It is often discussed in nutritional contexts due to its potential benefits. In the realm of infant nutrition, TAURINA may be added to infant formulas to support immune function and promote gastrointestinal development. Additionally, taurine is recognized for its use among athletes, as it may enhance physical performance. Overall, TAURINA is significant for both developmental and performance-related applications."}{"title": "GINSENG:Ginseng is an herbal supplement that may be used by athletes to enhance performance."}{"title": "INOSINA:Inosine is a supplement that may be used by athletes to improve performance."}{"title": "T\u00c9 VERDE:Green tea is a beverage that may be consumed by athletes for its potential performance-enhancing properties."}{"title": "AGENTES ALCALINIZANTES:Alkalizing agents, such as bicarbonate, are used by athletes to improve performance and delay fatigue."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTOS PROTEICOS:Protein supplements are used by athletes to enhance muscle growth and recovery."}{"title": "BETA-HIDROXI-BETA-METILBUTIRATO:Beta-hydroxy-beta-methylbutyrate (HMB) is a supplement used by athletes to promote muscle growth and recovery."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO LINOL\u00c9ICO CONJUGADO:El \u00e1cido linoleico conjugado (CLA) es un compuesto utilizado para la optimizaci\u00f3n del peso y la composici\u00f3n corporal."}{"title": "CART\u00cdLAGO DE TIBUR\u00d3N:El cart\u00edlago de tibur\u00f3n se utiliza para aumentar la resistencia a las lesiones y para la recuperaci\u00f3n de lesiones asociadas con el ejercicio."}{"title": "MUCOPOLISAC\u00c1RIDOS:Los mucopolisac\u00e1ridos son compuestos utilizados para la prevenci\u00f3n y recuperaci\u00f3n de lesiones en el \u00e1mbito deportivo."}{"title": "ARNICA:La \u00e1rnica es un compuesto utilizado para la recuperaci\u00f3n r\u00e1pida y completa de lesiones asociadas con el ejercicio."}{"title": "VITAMINAS C Y E:Las vitaminas C y E son compuestos antioxidantes utilizados para optimizar la recuperaci\u00f3n postejercicio."}{"title": "PROVITAMINA A:La provitamina A es un antioxidante utilizado para mejorar la recuperaci\u00f3n tras el ejercicio."}{"title": "N-ACETIL L-CISTE\u00cdNA:La N-acetil L-ciste\u00edna es un compuesto utilizado para mejorar la recuperaci\u00f3n tras el ejercicio."}{"title": "BIOFLAVONOIDES:Los bioflavonoides son compuestos utilizados para optimizar la recuperaci\u00f3n postejercicio."}{"title": "EQUINACEA:La equinacea es un inmunomodulador utilizado para mejorar la recuperaci\u00f3n tras el ejercicio."}{"title": "ESPIRULINA:La espirulina es un suplemento utilizado para optimizar la recuperaci\u00f3n postejercicio."}{"title": "\u0392-ALANINE:\u03b2-alanine is a nutritional supplement that can elevate muscle carnosine content, improving performance in high-intensity exercises."}{"title": "DOSIS DE MANTENIMIENTO:Dosis de mantenimiento refers to the daily dosage of supplements required to maintain satisfactory levels of phosphocreatine in the body."}{"title": "ALACTICO:"}{"title": "BETA-HIDROXI-METIL-BUTIRATO:Beta-hidroxi-metil-butirato (HMB) is a compound derived from leucine that plays an anabolic role in muscle preservation and is used to reduce muscle catabolism during exercise."}{"title": "DIRECCI\u00d3N GENERAL DE SALUD Y PROTECCI\u00d3N DEL CONSUMIDOR:The Direcci\u00f3n General de Salud y Protecci\u00f3n del Consumidor is a European Commission body that oversees health and consumer protection, including nutritional guidelines."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N DEPORTIVA INTENSIVA:Alimentaci\u00f3n deportiva intensiva involves specialized dietary strategies aimed at enhancing athletic performance during high-intensity training or competition."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N DEPORTIVA REGENERADORA:Alimentaci\u00f3n deportiva regeneradora focuses on nutrition strategies that aid recovery after exercise, helping athletes restore energy and repair muscle."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N DEPORTIVA:Nutrici\u00f3n deportiva encompasses the dietary practices and nutritional strategies specifically designed to support athletes' performance and recovery."}{"title": "DEPORTISTAS DE \u00c9LITE:Deportistas de \u00e9lite are elite athletes who engage in high-level competition and have specific nutritional needs due to their intense training regimens."}{"title": "NIVEL DE ACTIVIDAD:Nivel de actividad refers to the intensity and frequency of physical exercise that athletes engage in, influencing their nutritional requirements."}{"title": "CONCENTRACIONES DE VITAMINA D:Concentraciones de vitamina D refer to the levels of vitamin D in the body, which are critical for athletes' health and performance."}{"title": "EFECTOS PERJUDICIALES:Efectos perjudiciales refer to the negative impacts on muscle function and overall health that can occur when vitamin D levels are insufficient."}{"title": "NUEVAS INVESTIGACIONES:Nuevas investigaciones refer to ongoing studies aimed at understanding the relationship between vitamin D and athletic performance.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "HMB-CA:HMB-Ca is a form of Hydroxymethylbutyrate that is bound to calcium, mentioned in the context of nutritional supplementation for athletes."}{"title": "HMB-FA:HMB-FA is a free acid form of Hydroxymethylbutyrate, discussed as a nutritional supplement for optimizing athletic performance."}{"title": "PHILLIPS SM:Phillips SM is a researcher who has published studies on protein quality and its effects on muscle mass and weight loss in athletes."}{"title": "TAKANAMI Y:Takanami Y is a researcher who has investigated the benefits of vitamin E supplementation in endurance exercise."}{"title": "MACHEFER G:Machefer G is a researcher who has studied the impact of extreme running competitions on blood antioxidant defense capacity."}{"title": "VIITALA P:Viitala P is a researcher who has examined the relationship between vitamin E supplementation, exercise, and lipid peroxidation."}{"title": "PALACIOS N:Palacios N is a researcher who has contributed to various studies on nutritional ergogenic aids for athletes."}{"title": "CONSTANTINI NW:Constantini NW is a researcher focused on the iron status of highly active adolescents, particularly gymnasts."}{"title": "HOUTKOOPER L:Houtkooper L is a researcher who has explored eating disorders and disordered eating in athletes."}{"title": "SANBORN CHF:Sanborn ChF is a researcher who has studied disordered eating in female athletes."}{"title": "ANA ORTOL\u00c1 BUIGUES:Ana Ortol\u00e1 Buigues is a doctor and co-author of a study focused on water metabolism in patients receiving artificial nutrition. She has made significant contributions to the field of enteral nutrition through her research and studies."}{"title": "LUIS \u00c1NGEL CU\u00c9LLAR OLMEDO:Luis \u00c1ngel Cu\u00e9llar Olmedo is a medical professional specializing in the field of nutrition, with a particular focus on parenteral nutrition and access routes for enteral nutrition. He is associated with the Servicio de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n at Hospital Universitario R\u00edo Hortega, where he applies his expertise to improve nutritional care for patients."}{"title": "CONCEPCI\u00d3N TERROBA LARUMBE:Concepci\u00f3n Terroba Larumbe is a medical professional specializing in nutrition, particularly in enteral and parenteral nutrition access methods. She is associated with the Servicio de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n at Hospital Universitario R\u00edo Hortega, where she contributes to discussions and advancements in the field of nutrition."}{"title": "ANA ALEJANDRA CORDERO VAQUERO:Ana Alejandra Cordero Vaquero is a medical professional who specializes in nutrition, particularly in enteral and parenteral nutrition. She is associated with the Servicio de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n at Hospital Universitario R\u00edo Hortega, where she applies her expertise in providing nutritional support to patients."}{"title": "INTERNATIONAL SOCIETY OF SPORTS NUTRITION:The International Society of Sports Nutrition is an organization that provides guidelines and position stands on sports nutrition topics, including beta-hydroxy-beta-methylbutyrate (HMB)."}{"title": "SPORTS MEDICINE:Sports Medicine is a journal that focuses on the field of sports medicine, including research on dietary protein and its effects on athletes."}{"title": "STRENGTH & CONDITIONING RESEARCH:Strength & Conditioning Research is a journal that publishes studies on strength training, conditioning, and nutrition for athletes."}{"title": "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF APPLIED PHYSIOLOGY:The European Journal of Applied Physiology publishes research on the physiological aspects of exercise and nutrition."}{"title": "ARCHIVOS DE MEDICINA DEL DEPORTE:Archivos de Medicina del Deporte is a journal that focuses on sports medicine and nutrition for athletes."}{"title": "CLINICAL SPORTS NUTRITION:Clinical Sports Nutrition is a book that provides comprehensive information on nutrition for athletes, including dietary strategies and supplementation."}{"title": "NUTRITION AND SANT\u00c9 IBERIA, S.L.:Nutrition and Sant\u00e9 Iberia, S.L. is a company that focuses on dietary products and nutritional support for athletes."}{"title": "ARCH MED DEPORTE:Arch Med Deporte is a journal that publishes research related to sports medicine and nutrition."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF THE INTERNATIONAL SOCIETY OF SPORTS NUTRITION:The Journal of the International Society of Sports Nutrition publishes research on sports nutrition and dietary supplements for athletes."}{"title": "NUTRITION & METABOLISM:"}{"title": "ANA ORTOL\u00c1 BUIGES:Ana Ortol\u00e1 Buiges is a prominent figure in the field of clinical nutrition, specializing in immunonutrition and artificial nutritional support. As a doctor with expertise in nutrition, she actively engages in discussions surrounding enteral nutrition. Additionally, she is recognized as an author and contributor to both clinical and parenteral nutrition, highlighting her significant involvement and contributions to advancing knowledge in these areas."}{"title": "CENTRO DE INVESTIGACI\u00d3N ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:Centro de Investigaci\u00f3n Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n is a research center affiliated with the University of Valladolid, focusing on nutrition and metabolism."}{"title": "METABOLISMO H\u00cdDRICO:Metabolismo h\u00eddrico involves the processes of water balance and management in patients receiving artificial nutrition."}{"title": "NECESIDADES NUTRICIONALES:Las necesidades nutricionales son los requerimientos de nutrientes que pueden aumentar en ciertas condiciones m\u00e9dicas, lo que puede llevar a la necesidad de nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "DIARREA CUANTIOSA PERSISTENTE:La diarrea cuantiosa persistente es una condici\u00f3n caracterizada por evacuaciones intestinales frecuentes y abundantes que pueden afectar la salud del paciente."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL EXCLUSIVA:La nutrici\u00f3n enteral exclusiva es un enfoque de tratamiento que utiliza solo nutrici\u00f3n enteral para pacientes con condiciones espec\u00edficas, como la enfermedad de Crohn pedi\u00e1trica."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS SEVERAS:Las complicaciones infecciosas severas son efectos adversos que pueden surgir de la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral, aumentando el riesgo de infecciones en pacientes."}{"title": "ENTERITIS AGUDA GRAVE:"}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS DE NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL:Las f\u00f3rmulas de nutrici\u00f3n enteral son preparaciones dise\u00f1adas para proporcionar nutrientes a pacientes a trav\u00e9s de la alimentaci\u00f3n enteral, clasificadas en completas e incompletas nutricionalmente."}{"title": "DIARREAS:A condition that can be regulated with the use of specific nutritional formulas"}{"title": "MALTODEXTRINA:Maltodextrina, also known as maltodextrin, is a carbohydrate that serves as a vital energy source in various nutritional formulations. It is commonly utilized in enteral nutrition products, where it plays a significant role in providing energy to individuals who require nutritional support."}{"title": "CASE\u00cdNA HIDROLIZADA:Hydrolyzed casein, a protein source used in enteral nutrition"}{"title": "AISLADO DE PROTE\u00cdNA DE SOJA:Soy protein isolate, a protein source used in enteral nutrition"}{"title": "FIBRAS:"}{"title": "PREDI\u00c1LISIS:La predi\u00e1lisis es la fase anterior a la di\u00e1lisis en pacientes con enfermedad renal cr\u00f3nica, donde se requiere un manejo nutricional espec\u00edfico."}{"title": "OCFA:Obstructive Chronic Airflow Disease (OCFA) is a condition where specialized nutritional formulas may be indicated."}{"title": "FORMULAS NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional formulas are specialized products designed to meet the dietary needs of patients, particularly those unable to consume food orally."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA:F\u00d3RMULA es un sustituto de la leche materna utilizado para alimentar a los reci\u00e9n nacidos, especialmente aquellos que son prematuros. Esta f\u00f3rmula est\u00e1 dise\u00f1ada para satisfacer las necesidades nutricionales espec\u00edficas de estos infantes. Adem\u00e1s, las f\u00f3rmulas de nutrici\u00f3n enteral son preparaciones que proporcionan nutrientes a pacientes que no pueden alimentarse por v\u00eda oral, lo que resalta la versatilidad y la importancia de las f\u00f3rmulas en el \u00e1mbito de la nutrici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica y pedi\u00e1trica."}{"title": "SUEROTERAPIA:La sueroterapia es un m\u00e9todo de administraci\u00f3n de l\u00edquidos y nutrientes a trav\u00e9s de una v\u00eda venosa, complementando la nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA ESPECIAL:A specialized nutritional formula designed for patients with organ failure."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA ADAPTADA A PATOLOG\u00cdA:A nutritional formula adapted to specific medical conditions."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA OLIGOM\u00c9RICA:A type of nutritional formula that is partially hydrolyzed for easier absorption in patients with intestinal failure."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA NORMOPROTEICA:A nutritional formula containing a normal amount of protein, suitable for patients without severe stress."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA HIPERPROTEICA:A nutritional formula with a high protein content, used for patients under severe stress."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA NORMOCAL\u00d3RICA:A nutritional formula providing a normal caloric intake."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA HIPERCAL\u00d3RICA:A nutritional formula providing a high caloric intake for patients with increased energy needs."}{"title": "VAR\u00d3N DE 75 A\u00d1OS:A 75-year-old male patient admitted for medical treatment, potentially requiring nutritional support."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N CON JERINGA:A method of administering nutrition using a special syringe, typically delivering 200-300 ml per intake throughout the day."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N POR GRAVEDAD:A method of intermittent infusion that relies on gravity to regulate the flow of nutrition, typically administered 4-6 times a day."}{"title": "PRESCRIPCI\u00d3N DE NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL:The process of prescribing enteral nutrition, which must be standardized and precise to reduce errors in dispensing."}{"title": "MONITORIZACI\u00d3N DE NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL:The monitoring of enteral nutrition, focusing on the clinical and metabolic status of the patient and their tolerance to the nutritional preparation."}{"title": "VALORACI\u00d3N DE LA TOLERANCIA:The assessment of a patient's tolerance to enteral nutrition, which is crucial for effective treatment."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N INTERMITENTE:"}{"title": "REQUERIMIENTOS PROTEICOS:Los requerimientos proteicos son la cantidad de prote\u00ednas que el var\u00f3n de 75 a\u00f1os necesita diariamente, que se ha establecido en 70 g/d\u00eda."}{"title": "REQUERIMIENTOS H\u00cdDRICOS:Los requerimientos h\u00eddricos son la cantidad de l\u00edquidos que el var\u00f3n de 75 a\u00f1os necesita diariamente, que se ha establecido entre 2100-2800 ml/d\u00eda."}{"title": "BOLOS:Los bolos son una forma de administraci\u00f3n de nutrici\u00f3n enteral en la que se administran cantidades espec\u00edficas de alimento en intervalos regulares."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N DE LA TOLERANCIA:La evaluaci\u00f3n de la tolerancia es un proceso importante para determinar c\u00f3mo el var\u00f3n de 75 a\u00f1os est\u00e1 respondiendo a la nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS DEL PACIENTE:Los s\u00edntomas del paciente, como dolor abdominal y n\u00e1useas, son indicadores que se eval\u00faan para determinar la tolerancia a la nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "VARIABLES ANTROPOM\u00c9TRICAS:Las variables antropom\u00e9tricas, como el peso y los per\u00edmetros, son medidas que se revisan semanalmente en el var\u00f3n de 75 a\u00f1os para evaluar su estado nutricional."}{"title": "V\u00cdA ORAL:V\u00cdA ORAL refers to the method of nutrition that is being considered for a 75-year-old male patient once his condition allows for it. This approach aims to recover the oral feeding method, which some patients have transitioned to after ending their NPD (Nutritional Parenteral Diet) treatment."}{"title": "RESIDUO G\u00c1STRICO:El residuo g\u00e1strico se refiere a la cantidad de alimento o l\u00edquido que permanece en el est\u00f3mago despu\u00e9s de la alimentaci\u00f3n. Este volumen de contenido es importante para evaluar la tolerancia a la nutrici\u00f3n enteral, ya que su presencia puede indicar problemas de tolerancia. En pacientes que reciben nutrici\u00f3n enteral, el residuo g\u00e1strico se mide y se monitoriza para asegurar que el cuerpo est\u00e1 procesando adecuadamente los nutrientes."}{"title": "ESTRATEGIAS PARA REDUCIR EL RIESGO DE ASPIRACI\u00d3N:Son pr\u00e1cticas recomendadas para minimizar el riesgo de aspiraci\u00f3n en pacientes que reciben nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "BLOQUE SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO:"}{"title": "VACIADO G\u00c1STRICO:El vaciado g\u00e1strico es el proceso mediante el cual el contenido del est\u00f3mago se mueve hacia el intestino delgado, y es un factor cr\u00edtico en la nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICA DE ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N:La t\u00e9cnica de administraci\u00f3n se refiere a los m\u00e9todos utilizados para proporcionar nutrici\u00f3n enteral, incluyendo la posici\u00f3n del paciente y el ritmo de infusi\u00f3n."}{"title": "SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO:SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO refers to advanced nutritional support practices and protocols utilized in medical settings, particularly for patients in critical conditions. This approach encompasses various techniques aimed at managing the nutritional needs of patients, especially those requiring enteral and parenteral nutrition. It emphasizes the importance of catheter management and infection prevention to ensure patient safety and efficacy of nutritional support. Additionally, SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO focuses on the specific electrolyte and mineral requirements necessary for optimal patient care, while also addressing potential complications associated with parenteral nutrition. Overall, it plays a crucial role in influencing patient outcomes, including the management of conditions such as diarrhea."}{"title": "ANTIHIPERTENSIVOS:Antihypertensives are medications used to treat high blood pressure, which can have diarrhea as a side effect."}{"title": "COLINERGICOS:Cholinergics are drugs that can stimulate the parasympathetic nervous system and may cause diarrhea as a side effect."}{"title": "ANTIACIDOS CON MAGNESIO:Antacids containing magnesium can lead to diarrhea due to their laxative effect."}{"title": "ANTIDIABETICOS ORALES:Oral antidiabetic medications can cause gastrointestinal side effects, including diarrhea."}{"title": "INHIBIDORES DE LA RECAPTACION DE LA SEROTONINA:Serotonin reuptake inhibitors are antidepressants that can have gastrointestinal side effects, including diarrhea."}{"title": "FARMACOS QUIMIOTERAPICOS:Chemotherapeutic agents can cause various side effects, including diarrhea, due to their impact on rapidly dividing cells in the gastrointestinal tract."}{"title": "ANTIBIOTICOS:"}{"title": "FASCITIS NECROTIZANTE:Severe infection of the soft tissue that leads to necrosis, often occurring in patients with compromised immune systems."}{"title": "BENZODIACEPINAS:A class of medications that can contribute to constipation in patients, particularly the elderly."}{"title": "OPI\u00c1CEOS:Opioid medications that are commonly associated with causing constipation in patients."}&Å0␀␀␀␀␀–Ñ0␀␀␀␀␀ëá0␀␀␀␀␀à0␀␀␀␀␀•à0␀␀␀␀␀Iâ0␀␀␀␀␀Ωâ0␀␀␀␀␀@ä0␀␀␀␀␀ã0␀␀␀␀␀üã0␀␀␀␀␀vå0␀␀␀␀␀ç0␀␀␀␀␀êç0␀␀␀␀␀0é0␀␀␀␀␀Íé0␀␀␀␀␀Œè0␀␀␀␀␀wê0␀␀␀␀␀ë0␀␀␀␀␀Èë0␀␀␀␀␀ìí0␀␀␀␀␀Cì0␀␀␀␀␀ì0␀␀␀␀␀ïî0␀␀␀␀␀©î0␀␀␀␀␀¥ñ0␀␀␀␀␀Jò0␀␀␀␀␀ô0␀␀␀␀␀⁄ö0␀␀␀␀␀dõ0␀␀␀␀␀ú0␀␀␀␀␀òú0␀␀␀␀␀Iù0␀␀␀␀␀Îù0␀␀␀␀␀àû0␀␀␀␀␀Pü0␀␀␀␀␀N°0␀␀␀␀␀€°0␀␀␀␀␀Ò°0␀␀␀␀␀>§0␀␀␀␀␀3•0␀␀␀␀␀!¶0␀␀␀␀␀∑ß0␀␀␀␀␀Ãß0␀␀␀␀␀†®0␀␀␀␀␀X©0␀␀␀␀␀™0␀␀␀␀␀…™0␀␀␀␀␀Ö´0␀␀␀␀␀J¨0␀␀␀␀␀Ú¨0␀␀␀␀␀ß≠0␀␀␀␀␀VÆ0␀␀␀␀␀˙Æ0␀␀␀␀␀ªØ0␀␀␀␀␀Ú±0␀␀␀␀␀◊≤0␀␀␀␀␀ß≥0␀␀␀␀␀è¥0␀␀␀␀␀pµ0␀␀␀␀␀âµ0␀␀␀␀␀O∂0␀␀␀␀␀%∑0␀␀␀␀␀∏0␀␀␀␀␀Î∏0␀␀␀␀␀"ª0␀␀␀␀␀º0␀␀␀␀␀›º0␀␀␀␀␀åΩ0␀␀␀␀␀eæ0␀␀␀␀␀_ø0␀␀␀␀␀}ø0␀␀␀␀␀z¿0␀␀␀␀␀˙¬0␀␀␀␀␀¢√0␀␀␀␀␀zƒ0␀␀␀␀␀E≈0␀␀␀␀␀∆0␀␀␀␀␀ˆ«0␀␀␀␀␀ø»0␀␀␀␀␀W…0␀␀␀␀␀˙…0␀␀␀␀␀« 0␀␀␀␀␀`À0␀␀␀␀␀ıÀ0␀␀␀␀␀óÃ0␀␀␀␀␀`Õ0␀␀␀␀␀9Œ0␀␀␀␀␀Fœ0␀␀␀␀␀K“0␀␀␀␀␀”0␀␀␀␀␀¬”0␀␀␀␀␀‰”0␀␀␀␀␀’0␀␀␀␀␀≥’0␀␀␀␀␀C÷0␀␀␀␀␀∆÷0␀␀␀␀␀0◊0␀␀␀␀␀≈◊0␀␀␀␀␀Eÿ0␀␀␀␀␀Ãÿ0␀␀␀␀␀NŸ0␀␀␀␀␀jŸ0␀␀␀␀␀8⁄0␀␀␀␀␀⁄⁄0␀␀␀␀␀‹0␀␀␀␀␀ó‹0␀␀␀␀␀›0␀␀␀␀␀ç›0␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀àﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀ıﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀eﬂ0␀␀␀␀␀Íﬂ0␀␀␀␀␀C‡0␀␀␀␀␀ª‡0␀␀␀␀␀.·0␀␀␀␀␀≤·0␀␀␀␀␀%‚0␀␀␀␀␀õ‚0␀␀␀␀␀„0␀␀␀␀␀q„0␀␀␀␀␀Ù„0␀␀␀␀␀Q‰0␀␀␀␀␀´‰0␀␀␀␀␀	Â0␀␀␀␀␀`Â0␀␀␀␀␀—Â0␀␀␀␀␀9Ê0␀␀␀␀␀ñÊ0␀␀␀␀␀¸Ê0␀␀␀␀␀qÁ0␀␀␀␀␀…Á0␀␀␀␀␀?Ë0␀␀␀␀␀µË0␀␀␀␀␀CÈ0␀␀␀␀␀ÕÈ0␀␀␀␀␀‰È0␀␀␀␀␀™Í0␀␀␀␀␀&Î0␀␀␀␀␀µÎ0␀␀␀␀␀3Ï0␀␀␀␀␀¨Ï0␀␀␀␀␀Ì0␀␀␀␀␀àÌ0␀␀␀␀␀	Ó0␀␀␀␀␀àÓ0␀␀␀␀␀
